1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Magnus Bengtsson''' Minnesköld (Folkungaätten)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2nd Son of Earl Bengt Folkesson Snivel (Folkunga) and Sigrid Björnsdotter Lakman 
2 CONT * The Swedish Biographical Dictionary (SBL), and the Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters call him Magnus' memorial shield. Even Dick Harrison mentions him as Magnus Memory Shield. In Äldre Västgötalagen's lagm
2 CONC anslängd, the nickname is written in one place Minneskioldz , in another minniskiolz .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#BirgerBrosadied1202 Project MedLands, Sweden Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MAGNUS "Minnesköld" (-killed in battle near Lena 31 Jan 1208).  At Bjälbo.'''  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to th
2 CONC e monks of Juleta kloster[31].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum dux…Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjdem regis” donated propert
2 CONC y to Nydala kloster[32].  '''married firstly  ?.  The name of Magnus´s first wife is not known.  married secondly INGRID [Ylva]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus & his first wife had four children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''ESKIL Magnusson''' (-[1227]).  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[33].  Lag
2 CONC mand in Västergötland 1219/20.  '''married  (1217) as her second husband, KIRSTIN Nilsdotter,''' widow of HAAKON "Gallin" Jarl in Norway, daughter of NILS Blaka & his wife Katharina Eriksdotter of Sweden (-1254).
2 CONT
2 CONT * b)         [34] '''daughter''''  '''married SIGTRYGG Bengtson [Boberg] (-after 1219).''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * c)         '''KARL Magnusson''' (-killed in battle Rotala, Estonia 8 Aug 1220).  Bishop of Linköping.  Chancellor of Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * d)         '''ELOF Magnusson''' (-bur Alvästra Abbey).  1253/68  ''married ?''  (-bur Alvästra Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus & his second wife INGRID Ylva had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * e)         '''BENGT Magnusson''' (-4 Jan 1237).  Bishop of Linköping 1220.  m ---.  The name of Bengt´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bengt & his unknown wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>i)          '''MAGNUS Bengtsson''' (-1263).  Lagmand in Östergötland.  '''married RAGNHILD,''' daughter of (-1262).
2 CONT
2 CONT * f)          '''BIRGER Magnusson''' ([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Svecia" in 1248[35].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founde
2 CONC r of Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Directory of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=9&postid=sdhk_216&tab=post#tab 216]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1184 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Knut announces that he as alms donated 2 whole bol (mansiunculas) in fishing1 in Älvkarleby to the Cistercian monks in Julita and their descendants. The witnesses were Archbishop Stefan in Uppsala, Bishop Vilhelm in Strängnäs
2 CONC , Duke Birger, his brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryker, Sven "owin", "Syctrig brown" and several other great men in the country, clerks and laymen. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006283701220?album_type=photos_of_me
2 CONC &photo_id=6000000138144517866
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=11&postid=sdhk_268&tab=post#tab 268]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating 1192 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Knut Eriksson to gentlemen and great men with confirmation of their sale of a third in the fishing lake Sken for three land gold to Nydala monastery. The purchase is confirmed by Bishop Kol, Earl Birger, King's brother Filip,
2 CONC  Earl's brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryk, the monks Peter Albus and Peter from Norway, the custodian Torald and Styrger's son Tove and the play brothers Hagbard, Gjord and Åke. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006283
2 CONC 701220?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000138144942831
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=12&postid=sdhk_287&tab=post#tab 287]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating 1200 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sverker Karlsson to the 'princes and the great men' with confirmation of the sale of a third in the fishing lake Sken for three land gold to Nydala monastery and its legal possession thereof. The purchase is confirmed by Bish
2 CONC op Kol, Earl Birger, King Knut's brother Philip, the Earl's brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryk, the monks Peter Albus and Peter from Norway, the custodian Torald and Styrger's son Tove and the play brothers Hagbard, Gjord and 
2 CONC Åke. Whoever puts obstacles in the way of this is threatened with banishment, and the king urges his successors not to decrease but to increase the support of God's servants.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Medieval transcripts:  Vid. Perg. 13720509 - Contents Off. 12210000 (DS 833) and 12220000 (DS 834), Shoester Monastery, RA 0107.14. Post-medieval transcripts:  Örnhielm: VIII p. 406 (e. Or. And vid.)
2 CONT
