2 CONT ==Chapter 3.    KINGS of SWEDEN 1250-1412 (FOLKINGAÄTTEN)==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIRGER Magnusson, son of MAGNUS "Minnesköld" [Folkungaätten] & his second wife Ingrid [Ylva] ([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).'''  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Sv
2 CONC ecia" in 1248[173].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founder of Stockholm.  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj
2 CONC  ac Benedictj Scolaris”[174].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1265 of "Birgerus dux Sveciæ"[175]. '''married firstly ([1235]) INGEBORG of Sweden, daughter of ERIK Knutsson King of Sweden & his second wife Richeza of Denm
2 CONC ark ([1212]-17 Jun 1254)'''.  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 4 Nov 1246 in which “Ericus…rex Swethie” names “domino Birgero genero nostro”[176].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified
2 CONC .  '''married secondly (1261) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Holstein, widow of ABEL King of Denmark, daughter of ADOLF IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe (1225-1288, bur Varnhem Abbey).'''  The Ann
2 CONC ales Stadenses record the marriage "1237 VII Kal Mai" of "dux Abel" and "filiam comitis Adolfi de Scowenborch", naming her "Mechtildem" and recording her second marriage to "ducem Sueciæ" in a later passage[177].  The Icelandic An
2 CONC nals record the marriage in 1261 of "Bergerus Sveciæ dux" and "Mathildam reginam Daniæ"[178].  '''Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Birger's mistress is not known.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson & his first wife INGEBORG of Sweden had eight children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''RIKISSA Birgersdotter''' (-before 13 Dec 1288).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Rixam filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Henricum seniorem [filium Nycolai domini de Werle]"[179].  The primary source which confi
2 CONC rms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  m firstly (Oslo 1251) HAAKON Haakonsson "den Unge/the Young" under King of Norway, son of HAAKON IV "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wife Margareta Skulesdotter (Bergen 
2 CONC 10 Nov 1232-Tønsberg 30 Apr or 5 May1257, bur Oslo, St Hallvards Church).  m secondly (1262) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Werle, son of NIKOLAUS I Herr von Werle zu Rostock [Mecklenburg] & his wife Jutta von Anhalt (-murdered n
2 CONC ear Saal, Rügen 8 Oct 1291).  Herr zu Werle zu Güstrow 1281. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''VALDEMAR Birgersson''' ([1237]-Nyköping Castle 26 Dec 1302).  The Icelandic Annals record that "Valdemarus Birgiri filius" succeeded as king of Sweden in 1249[180].  He succeeded in 1250 as VALDEMAR King of Sweden.
2 CONC   “Waldemarus…rex Swechie” confirmed the donation of property to Gudhems Kloster by “reginam dominam Katerinam” by charter dated 17 Jan 1251 which names “patris nostri domini Byrgerj ducis”[181].  The Annales Lubicenses records th
2 CONC at "Waldemarus rex Sweorum" was deposed in 1275 by "Magno duce fratre suo"[182].  The Icelandic Annals record the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus" and the departure of Valdemar for Denmark soon after[183].  The I
2 CONC celandic Annals record the death in 1302 of "Valdemarus Birgeri filius Rex Sveonum"[184].  ''''married  firstly (1260, divorced after 1276) SOPHIE of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of S
2 CONC axony (-1286).'''  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[185].  The Icelandic Annals note the presenc
2 CONC e of "Sophia regina Valdimari regis, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[186].  '
2 CONC ''married secondly LUCARDIS, daughter of ---.  1296.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.'''   '''Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife
2 CONC  Jutta of Saxony ([1246]-[1286/95]).'''  Abbess of St Agneta in Roskilde 1266.  She left the convent in 1271[187]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' King Valdemar had & his first wife SOPHIE of Denmark had seven children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' (-1261, bur Sigruna Abbey).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>* b)        ''' INGEBORG Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1290]).  The Annales Lubicenses refer to the first wife of "Gherardi comitis Holtzatiæ" as "filia Woldemari Regis Sweciæ"[188].  “Waldemarus…Rex Sveorum” confirmed a grant to Hamb
2 CONC urg by “pater noster Dominus Byrgerus felicis memoriæ Dux Sveorum” by charter dated 12 Dec 1275 “in nuptiis filiæ nostræ…et comitis Gerardi…de Holsatia”[189].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia regina Valdimari reg
2 CONC is, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[190].  '''married  (12 Dec 1275) as his f
