2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Riddare Halsten Petersson Halv Lilja and Märta Knutsdotter (Tre rosor), till Mörby 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Knut Halstensson (half lily) was married to [https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halsten_Peterssons_%C3%A4tt '''Katarina Guttormsdotter,'''] daughter of Guttorm Toresson (split shield) and Inga Gregersdotter ( Malstaätten )
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Catalog of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=9347&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_10897&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab '''SDHK no: 10897''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 October 26'''
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: Uppsala''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Knut Halstensson announces that in the presence of Gisle Uddsson and Nils Petersson in Länna, on behalf of his wife Katarina Guttormsdotter, he has agreed with Archbishop Birger (Gregersson) in Uppsala and Kettil Johansson rega
2 CONC rding the estate and possessions that his wife inherited from her mother Inga Gregersdotter, wife Katarina ( Johansdotter) in Sund and Bishop Tomas in Växjö, all deceased. The testator and his wife receive 6 demesne and 6 1/2 öres
2 CONC land of land, namely in Utlunda in (Roslags-) Bro parish 22 öresland and five crofts below it and the island of Idö in Vätö parish, in Morberga in Bälinge parish 14 öresland, in Malsta (in Malsta parish) 1 land, in Sund in (Roslag
2 CONC s-) Bro parish 6 öresland and in Torsholma in Frösunda parish 4 1/2 öresland. The issuer admits on behalf of his wife to have borne all this and acknowledges Archbishop Birger and Kettil Johansson.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The letter is sealed by the knights Karl Ulfsson, lawman in Uppland, Arvid Gustavsson, lawman in Österland, and the men-at-arms Gisle Uddsson and Nils Petersson.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Post-medieval transcripts:'''  Transcript - with the postscript "Concordat cum vero origenali a verbo ad verbum vna cum sigillis" - in Nicol. Rabenii collections, Skokl. In Fol., vol. 216 (E 8883), no. 63 (loose sheet), Sv. T
2 CONC he National Archives.Post-medieval regest/notice:  List in 1561 of Gustaf Johansson's (Tre Rosor) land deed, U 303 a fol. B 9, KB
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Additional Text:''' On the back of the sheet: En wiss copia vdaff dito pergamentz schifftes bref emellenn Knuth Hallstensson and archbishop Birger j Vpsala and Kættill Joansson as him on his husfrws wægne æffter des moder sampt
2 CONC  and husfrw Katrine j Sunde and æffter biscop Tomas j Wexiø ærffue borde and de sigh der om förient's haffue. And with Mr. Carl Vlffson's lagman j Vplandh, jtem Mr. Arffuedh Gustaffsson's lagman j Østerlandh, Gisla Vdsson's and Ni
2 CONC clas Petersson's hanging jnsegler confirmed. The date Vpsala MCCCLxx sexto, xxvj die mensis Octobris. Below: If Vthlunda and fæm thorp there vnder jnnan Bro soknn, along with Jdøøn j Wætø soknn and some more goods.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SEAL Seal drawings:''' no. 1 round (shield without pictorial content, see SMV II, p. 484 and preserved e.g. in letter 1372 16/6, DS X, no. 172 and 1385 13/1, RPB no. 2074): Knut Halstenson; no. 2 round (heraldic seal, see SMV I
2 CONC , p. 118 and preserved e.g. in letter 1374 8/9, DS no. 8639): + S' ‧ Karoli ‧ Wlphs on militia; no. 3 round (heraldic seal, see SMV I, p. 119 and preserved e.g. for letter 1373 11/10, DS X, no. 261 and letter 1375 12/11, DS no. 88
2 CONC 69): S Arvidi ‧ Gostafson; No. 4 round (heraldic seal): S' Niklai Peterson; No. 5 round (heraldic seal): S' ‧ Gislonis ‧ Vdson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=100&Sokord=forn%C3%A5sa&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettLimits=zfSYjA%3A0&AvanceradSok=False&page=15&postid=sdhk_10962&tab=post '''SDHK no: 10962''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1377 March 5'''
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: Sundby in Forsa parish''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Halstensson issues a letter regarding the land exchange that Mr. Lidinvard Haraldsson made on behalf of the issuer in Forsa with the issuer's mother Mrs. Märta Knutsdotter and his brother in the presence of Bishop Tomas in V
2 CONC äxjö, Johan Gregersson and Mr. Peter in By, '''regarding both the fathers, mothers and mother's morning gift. The executor divides the previously undivided estate with his mother and his brother Knut Halstensson in such a way that
2 CONC  he transfers to them his entire property in Fornåsa in Boberg's county in exchange for their entire property in Lower and Upper Götala in Styra parish.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals together with the knights Ragvald Magnusson and Ingevald Anundsson and with Mr. Jakob i Forsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources - Post-medieval transcripts:  Transcript - under the heading "Bytes bref opå Fornusum in Boberss heradh medh Nidhra och Öffra Götalum etc. 1377." - in Lars Eriksson Sparre's copybook B 15, fol. 11r, RA 0202'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halsten_Peterssons_%C3%A4tt Halsten Petersson's Family, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Halsten Petersson's family ,''' also called half lily , is a contemporary conventional name for a Swedish medieval squire family that took its name from the progenitor, knight and bailiff Halsten Petersson. The family died out 
2 CONC before Sweden's Riddarhus was founded in 1625, which is why it was never introduced there as nobility . The members of the family wore a red scotch, with half a golden lily laid in beams in the upper field.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Two land exchanges from 1377 and 1380 give good insight into the mutual kinship of several members.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family Tree'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Halsten Petersson, knight (1355),''' landowner and bailiff. His origin is unknown, but a (half) brother is mentioned, Arvid Petersson, who carried a spar in the coat of arms. 1336 and 1338 goods as thanks for faithful service
2 CONC . he was given by King Magnus Eriksson but participated in King Erik Magnusson 's rebellion against his father, and is mentioned among Erik's five pledges in 1357, but is stated to have died on March 1, 1358. [ 3 ] '''Married Märt
2 CONC a (Margareta) Knutsdotter ( Tre Rosor till Mörby ), daughter to Knut (Tre Rosor till Mörby) and Kristina Bengtsdotter in Haneström, daughter of the lawman in Västergötland Bengt Hafridsson .''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1- '''Johan Halstensson'''
2 CONT >>>* 1- '''Halsten Johansson.''' According to Peder Månsson Utter (1566-1623) in ( Collectanea genealogica ), Halsten Johansson carried a fragmented shield with the upper half of a split (not split) lily gilt in the upper field. A
2 CONC ccording to the same source, Halsten was the father of Håkan Halstensson. 
2 CONT >>>>>* 1- '''Håkan Halstensson,''' knight, named 1346-1380. [ 8 ] Married to Bengta, daughter of the knight and councilor Sigge Magnusson ( Vinstorpaätten , Håkan Tunesson's family ) and Ramborg. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* 1 '''NN Håkansdotter,''' married to Ulf Bengtsson ( Sparre of Hjulsta and Ängsö ), parents of, among others, Bishop Sigge in Strängnäs.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* 2 - '''Sven Jonsson (half lily) til Dinglevik,''' Steneby, died about 1484, was a gunsmith and signed up to Dingelvik , which was a salvation farm , later a manor in ( Steneby parish ), and married on 5 October 1449 [ 11 ] at
2 CONC  Stola with an Ingeborg Bytesdotter, the daughter of Tore Byting . 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>'''Three children are known:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* '''Ragnhild Svensdotter (half lily)
2 CONT >>>>* '''Karin Svensdotter (half lily)''' to Dinglevik, Steneby.'''
2 CONT >>>>* '''Botilla Svensdotter (half lily)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2 - '''Thord Halstensson'''
2 CONT * 3 - '''Knut Halstensson (half lily)''' was married to Katarina Guttormsdotter, daughter of Guttorm Toresson (split      shield) and Inga Gregersdotter ( Malstaätten )
2 CONT * 4 - '''Håkan Hallstensson''' During the civil war in 1364, had his estates confiscated by King Håkan Magnusson , which Håkan gave to Nils Bengtsson (Lion-faced, Bengt Nilsson's family)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Literature and commentary, About Lidinvard Haraldsson (Lidinvard Haraldsson's family) see ÄSF I, p. 101 f.
2 CONT About Märta Knutsdotter (three roses) and her two sons Håkan and Knut in the marriage with Halsten Petersson (half lily), see H. Gillingstam, Ätterna Oxenstierna ud Vasa und medeltiden (1952), p. 47 f. and p. 739 with note 58; abo
2 CONC ut wife Märta see also ÄSF II, p. 87 f. About Peter, parish priest in By and canon in Västerås and Växjö, see G. Ekström, Västerås stifts herdaminne I:1 (1939), pp. 507 f. with mention of this letter. See also letter 13701028 (DS 
2 CONC no. 8228; SDHK no. 9819 ).
2 CONT * Literature and commentary, The letter is also available in another copy - under the heading "Böthess letter om arffgodz mellen Katerina Gudtormissdotter and archiebiscop Byrger's sister daughter on 27 markland 8 1/2 ortugland 3 
2 CONC penningland iord" - in Lars Eriksson Sparre's copy book B 15, fol. 274v, Sv. The National Archives. However, the transcript begins as the next DS no. 9348 (which deals with another part of the same inheritance), thus with Birger G
2 CONC regersson and Kettil Johansson as issuers; the place of issue is also the same as in this letter. In fact, the text in B 15 should probably be regarded as a summary of (parts of) the content of both of these letters. In the headin
2 CONC g (see above) they have also added up the total amount of land of the shifted estate, which should however amount to only 27 land and 3 money land. Regarding the inheritance, see comments and literature references at the nearest D
2 CONC S no. 9348. Regarding Österland, see comment to DS no. 9206. See ÄSF I:2, p. 176 f. The Malsta family. See deed of probate 1376 27/10 (transcript B 15 f. 274v, RA 0202)
2 CONT * Printed regestList in 1561 of Gustaf Johansson's (Tre roros) land deed, published by KH Karlsson in Västergötland's Fornminnesförenings Tidskrift 2, booklet 8-9 (1908), p. 148.
