1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Bengt Magnusson (Folkungaättens lagmansgren)==
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Magnusson (son of Magnus Bengtsson, tab. 11). Was the layman in Östergötland, mentioned as such for the first time in 1269. Mentioned as a member of the Swedish National Council on September 11, 1288. Must have taken off on 
2 CONC pilgrimage in 1289. Again active as a layman in 1291-1292. It is said to have died in 1294, which, however, seems to be in conflict with the fact that his son Magnus is mentioned as lawman already in 1293. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriages==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1) '''Margareta,''' possibly born from Tjust, who was dead in 1275, when the husband of, among others. a. The salvation of her soul donated property in Östergötland and in Tjust hd in Småland to a canonate in Linköping
2 CONC , 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (2) '''Sigrid the Fair,''' who died in 1289 and is buried in Skänninge dominican monastery. According to Margareta Klausdotter's familiar, partly purely historical story"Sigrid the fair" of lower burden than the man.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Magnus Bengtsson''' According to Ericus Olai, he became lawman in Östergötland at his father's departure from the kingdom in 1289. In that case, he must have resigned the office by 1291 but is mentioned again in 1293 as la
2 CONC wman, when he is titled "dominus M. legifer osgothorum" and even placed before Marshal Tyrgils Knutsson. Certainly died before 1304, when the office was held by a deputy.
2 CONT * 2. '''Ingeborg Bengtsdotter,''' Died in September 1314 and buried in Uppsala Cathedral. According to her will on the deathbed, a number of grants would be paid to Uppsala Cathedral and several monasteries. The inheritance after 
2 CONC her was changed in 1320. Apart from a few difficult-identified properties, it consisted of land in Aspelands, Handburds, Sevede and Stranda hd, all in Småland. Was 20.2 1301 married to the lawman in Uppland the knight and the nati
2 CONC onal council Birger Petersson ( Finstaätten ) to Finsta, who was previously married to Kristina Johansdotter, who died in 1293 and was the daughter of the knight Johan Elofsson (the family of the Elof Sons ) and his wife, a daught
2 CONC er of Mr Karl Tjelvason ( Fånöätten). Mr. Birger died on 3.4 1327. In the marriage between him and Ingeborg Bengtsdotter was born, among other things. a. the holy Birgitta.
2 CONT * 2. '''Ramborg Bengtsdotter,''' First mentioned in 1313 and then called wife. Lived another 1349. Buried in Riseberga monastery. Owned property in Grimsten's hd in Närke and Lysings hd in Östergötland. According to Margareta Klau
2 CONC sdotter, he was married to an otherwise unknown Erengisl, who apparently died long before his wife and is said to have been buried in Svanhals in Lysings hd in Östergötland.
2 CONT * 2. '''Katarina Bengtsdotter,''' Stayed another 1350 at Aspenäs in Malexander's snow in Outer hd in Östergötland. Sold, for example, with his children 's consent Rönnäs in Asby snow in the same height. Was 5.9 1319, well for a lo
2 CONC ng time, married to the knights knight Knut Jonsson ( Aspenäsätt ), who is mentioned as living 1292–1345 but was dead 18.3 1347.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
