1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Sigge Guttormsson''', till Ljuna=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Guttorm Guttormsson and Eldrid Jonsdatter 
2 CONT * Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna was a Swedish stormman from Hogstad parish near Mjölby in Östergötland, died 1283 who is considered the grandson of Earl Guttorm . He was married to Birger Jarls daughter Kristina Birgersdotter (died 1
2 CONC 285).
2 CONT * Birth:	after circa 1220 Sverige
2 CONT * Death: 1283
2 CONT *  Buried: Alvastra Monastery
2 CONT * Guttormsson to Ljuna was a Swedish Greatman from Hogstad near Mjölby in Östergötland, Dead 1283 who is considered the grandson of Guttorm Jarl. He was married to Birger Jarl 's daughter Kristina Birger's daughter (d. 1285). 
2 CONT * Seat yard: Ljuna in Hogstad
2 CONT * Sigge Guttormsson was the stormman in Östergötland in the 13th century, living in Hogstad near Mjölby. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: '''Kristina Birgersdotter,''' in her second marriage. married to Birger Jarl 's daughter Kristina Birgersdotter. The storm in Östergötland in the 13th century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birger Siggesson gumsehuvud; A son is also known through Sigge Guttormsson's will, written 11 June 1283. '''To his son Birger as the "schooling" the value of his own armor, since it was sold by the testament dean Dean Jng (e 
2 CONC / mouth /?). The young son Birger gets his father's armor, because he seems to be dedicated to a worldly career as a knight. 
2 CONT * '''Helena Siggesdotter; '''Their daughter Helena's daughter is to have been married first to the Danish knight Ingemar Nielsen, and Then to Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). A son is also known by Siggy Guttormssons Testament, written 11 J
2 CONC une 1283.
2 CONT * '''Margaret Siggesdotter''' Their daughter Margareta Kristinadotter was married to the lawyer Leonard Ödesson (Örnfot).
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=20&Sokord=Kristina&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettLimits=IfjiTQ%3A0&AvanceradSok=True&page=11&postid=sdhk_992&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 
2 CONC '''992''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1276 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge to Ljuna and his wife Kristina bequeath their farm in Västra Ljuna (Hogstad parish) with all movable and immovable property to Alvastra monastery, where they choose their burial place, to help the monks there, on condition t
2 CONC hat they pay what the issuer owes for two eights in said yard. In addition, the issuers stipulate that no heir after their death can revoke the testamentary gift, unless they have jointly agreed during the issuers' lifetime to red
2 CONC eem it. The witnesses were the abbot Johannes, the cellar master Olof and the monks Gudmund and Stenar in the said monastery, and the sailors were i.a. King M (agnus) and Bishop H (enrik) in Linköping.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000025565454677&photo_id=6000000178117599970&position=0 '''SEAL: All 5 seals lost; to 4 are the silk threads left.''']  Printed DS 608
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=sigge+guttormsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_1238&tab=post#tab 1238]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000025565454677&photo_id=6000000138090200144&position=0 '''Issued: 12830611'''] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents: Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna prepares his will as follows: to the monks in Alvastra, where he chooses his grave, he donates his farm in Västra Ljuna (Hogstads parish) with movable property in accordance with a previous let
2 CONC ter (12760000 b, DS 608), to the church of Näsby's estate, comprising a tooth of any new cultivation, to Salmundus, the parish priest in the church, 1 land of money, to the church in Hogstad (Hogstad parish) 1/4 eighth in "Colstho
2 CONC rp" to cover the expenses of someone Sister Priest there, to Mr. Runstanus, Sister Priest there, 2 Mark Pence, to the Lesser Brothers in Söderköping 1 Mark Silver, to the Preacher Brothers in Skänninge 1 Mark Silver, to the Preach
