2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd Haraldsson or Sigurd Munn (old Norse Sigurðr Haraldsson (1133–1155) was king of Norway from 1136 to 1155. He was son of Harald Gille, king of Norway and his mistress Tora Guttormsdotter (Þóra Guthormsdóttir). He ruled as co
2 CONC -ruler with his brothers, Inge Haraldsson and Eystein Haraldsson. His epithet Munn means "the Mouth" in Old Norse. He was killed in the power-struggle against his brother, Inge, in an early stage of the civil war era in Norway.
2 CONT
