2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 without day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Information about a letter in which Per Karlsson, Dan Karlsson, Ragvald Nilsson, Gregers Karlsson, Ingrid Karlsdotter and their mother Ingeborg Magnusdotter divided the inheritance after their father Carl Dansson. One lot fell to 
2 CONC wife Ingrid and wife Ingegerd, "another Gregers, third Daan and fourth Mr. Peder".
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Post-medieval regest/notice:  Genealogica 41, fol. 173r, RA
2 CONT
2 CONT Carii Daanson 1341. g(x) : Mrs. Ingeborgh Magnusadotter Carll Månson's sister 1358 widow. (three times gin-stitched shield)”Raguall Nilson [:]Carll Danson calls him(l) magh 1354 and Daan Karlson 1358. DS 5838 b  see pdf of print L
2 CONC iterature and commentary see DS no. 5838 b
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225627773924&size=large}} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk/?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=11853&Innehall=++&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermed
2 CONC eltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_11853&tab=post#tab SDHK number: 11853]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1381 February 26, : Place of issue: Outlaw Köping (Köping)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Content'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The marshal of the realm, knight Sten Bengtsson, the drost in Sweden Bo Jonsson, Folke Nilsson and Peter Djäken , under-secretary in Södermanland on behalf of Mr. Knut Karlsson, issue a writ of judgment. King Albrekt has in an ope
2 CONC n letter given the writsmen Folke Nilsson and Peter Djäken the authority to resolve a dispute between Ragvald Nilsson and Harald Kase regarding the property that Karl Dansson and his wife mortgaged to their son-in-law Bengt Larsso
2 CONC n. After examining the open letters of both sides and taking into account all the information they have obtained and heard, they cannot find anything other than that the property rightfully belongs to Ragvald Nilsson and those who
2 CONC  own the land with him. The writsmen therefore give the property to Ragvald Nilsson and reject Harald Kase's claim. The judgment is pronounced in the presence of the knights Erengisle Sunesson Earl, Bo Bosson, Birger Ulfsson, Staf
2 CONC fan Ulfsson and Anund Jonsson and the squires Lars Björnsson and Ulf Jonsson. The issuers, knight Sten Bengtsson and drost Bo Jonsson, declare that Ragvald Nilsson and Harald Kase appeared before them at the same place, whereupon 
2 CONC Harald Kase was requested to completely renounce the property, and Ragvald Nilsson shall have no further claims on Harald Kase after this day. Thus they shall be in agreement and the dispute resolved. The issuers seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Original:  Orig. on parchment (27.3 x 15.1 cm, fold 3.4 cm; 17 lines), Swedish National Archives (SE/RA/0101)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Post-medieval copies:  Misc. 74:3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT All the men who theta bref hear æll see how we Sten Beniczson ride e oc the march of the kingdom Bo Jonsson drozate j Swerike ‧ Folke Nicliss on ‧ oc Pæthar Dyekn vnd e rlaghman j Sudherma n na land e ‧ a ‧ h her ra Knwt Karlss on
2 CONC  s weghna æu e rdhelika m æth waro m Her ra ‧ Æpter thẏ høghborin første war kær e h er ra konu n g Albricht os Folka Nicliss on oc Pæthar e Dẏekn forsc ri phno m bøth oc befelde j sino opno breue ransaka oc vtleta ‧ sa n nẏnd oc 
2 CONC ræt vm the gothza delo who has been hafu e r mello m Raghuald Nicliss on oc Harald Kasa ‧ vm the gothz ther Karl Danss on oc hans wife hafdho pantsat thera magh Bæinct Lafrinzson oc os macht them mæth ræt atskilia ‧ gaf j samu bre
2 CONC fue tha hafuom wi thet ransakat oc vtleet ‧ æpt e r beggias thera opno brefuom oc m æth allom thøm bæzto m schælo m wi condom th e r til fa ælla høra ‧ oc æpter waro bæzto sa m witi so m wi viliom for e Gudhi ken nas tha wito m wi
2 CONC  eẏ rættar e æn thet sama gothz rætlika belongs to thøm forsc ri phna Raghwalde Nicliss on oc thøm th et agaar m æth ho no m . And for thẏ hafuo m wi Raghwalde Nicl is on th the same gothz tilvnnet oc toll from ‧ oc vndan Harald e
2 CONC  Kasa before erlikr a manna where her ra Eringisl e Sonas on s iærls sin ‧ her ra Bo Bosons ‧ her ra Birgher e Vlfsons ‧ her ra Staphan Vlfs on s ‧ and her ra Anu n dz Jonssons knights Lafrinz Biornss ons oc Vlf Jons on s swe na .
2 CONC  O ke n no m ps wi Sten Beniczson riddar a oc Bo Jonsson drotzte forsc ri phne at ther æpter a sama stath gingo the for nemp de Ragwal[ d ] Nicliss on oc Harald Kase for e eet mẏnne oc sæmio sculd til waar oc wi them for mynne sak
2 CONC t hafwm at Harald Kase scall ganzklika aflata thet sama gothz her til j delo standet hafu e r mello m hans oc Ragwald Nicliss on oc he m affonet war and Raghwalder Niclisson shall no indictment hafua until then for nemp da Harald 
2 CONC Kasa vm thet he opb[ out ]it hafu e r of thøm same research ri phna gothzom till that day. Oc ther mæth sculu the wara ‧ vinlika vm thessa gothza deelo excused. Oc til thessa thinga ‧ meere wisso oc witnisbẏrdh hafuom wi latet war
2 CONC  incighle her for e hænght. Date Laghløsakøpu n g, anno Domini Mccclxxxjº, feria tercia proxima post diem beati Mathie apostoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT * On the back: Eth dom breff, SEAL Seal: no. 1 only strip; no. 2 round of uncolored wax, diameter 3.0 cm (heraldic seal, see SMV I, p. 408): […]oecii Ionson; no. 3–4 only notches, DS no. 10340   see pdf of print Printed register R
2 CONC PB 1562
2 CONT * '''Literature and commentary:''' For the authors Sten Bengtsson (Bielke) and Folke Nilsson (Ivar Nilsson's family) see SRM with further references; for Peter (Torstensson) Djäken (Schack of Skylvalla), underling on behalf of Knu
2 CONC t Karlsson (Sparre of Tofta; see SRM p. 55), see J. E. Almquist in Släkt och hävd 1960, pp. 6 f. and p. 24, and the same in Lagsagor och domsagor i Sverige I (1954), p. 97, note 1. About the disputants, see for the squire Ragvald 
2 CONC Nilsson (Fargalt) ÄSF I, p. 30, and for Harald Kase ÄSF I, p. 299 f. About the witnesses Erengisle Sunesson (boat), titular earl of the Orkney Islands, Bo Bosson (Night and Day), Birger Ulfsson (Ulfåsaätten), Staffan Ulfsson (Wolf
2 CONC ), Anund Jonsson (Lion Face), Lars Björnsson (beam) and Ulf Jonsson (Aspenäsätten), see SRM with further references.
2 CONT The place of issue Köping is written in the letter Laglösaköping; on this name see H. Lindroth in Fornvännen 1918, pp. 213–223, and Swedish Place Name Dictionary (2016), p. 192 (under Köping). A large stain (which occupies about ⅓
2 CONC  of the letter) has made parts of the text only readable under UV light (see notes).
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225623140063&size=large}} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources Original: Or. perg., RA 0101 images, Post-medieval transcripts: Hadorph: E 80, p. 27, No. 13; Örnhielm: Misc. 4:14
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Folkunga%C3%A4ttens_o%C3%A4kta_gren The Illegitimate Branch of the Folkunga Family, by Adelsvapen Geneologies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 3'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Gregersson''' (son of Gregers, tab. 1). Mentioned 19.10 1285. Was a squire in 1286 and a knight in 1288. Apparently belonged to King Birger's council already in 1291 and in any case in 1299. Was a magistrate in Västmanla
2 CONC nd in 1305. Mentioned as alive at the latest 13.12 1319. Died 9.1 1326 and buried with the Dominicans in Sigtuna. Had ancestral estates on Arnö in Övergrans sn in Håbo hd in Uppland, which he sold to Uppsala Cathedral. Owned Brunn
2 CONC sholm in Näs sn in Åsunda hd in Uppland as well as several landed properties on Ängsö in the same sn in Yttertjurbo hd in Västmanland, which he exchanged for land in Vallentuna hd in Uppland. Also owned scattered goods in Rasbo, H
2 CONC agunda, Ulleråkers and Vaksala hd in Uppland. '''Married for the first time after 27.9 1282 but before 10.12 1288 to Ragnhild Erlandsdotter who was the daughter of Mr. Erland Israelsson ( Finstaätten ) and Katarina Johansdotter ( 
2 CONC Ängel ), and who had previously been married to Mr. Johan Karlsson (Fånöätten), executed in 1280.''' She made her will on 10.12 1288 and then chose her camp town with the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. Magnus Gregersson was then, b
2 CONC efore 4.11 1295, '''remarried to Ingegärd Filipsdotter, daughter of the knight Filip Finvidsson ( Rumbyätten ) and a daughter of Karl Tjelvason ( Fånöätten ).''' Ingegärd made her will as a widow in 1326 and chose her camp town wi
2 CONC th the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. Still alive on 16.2.1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peter Magnusson.''' Was a minor in 1298 and still in 1302. Died 3.12.1310, when he was buried and his father made his will, in which the churches in Fittja in Lagunda hd in Uppland and in Aspö in Selebo hd in Södermanland 
2 CONC were assigned as a legacy, where he apparently owned property. The farm Dalby in Aspö sn in Selebo hd was also determined as a pledge for the legacy. Owned maternal land in Frötuna shipbuilding in Uppland. Inherited from his mater
2 CONC nal uncle, the canon Karl Erlandsson, land in Färentuna hd in Uppland. In 1310, he ceded land in Frösåkers and Färentuna hd in Uppland to the Sko monastery for atonement of committed violence in Svartlösa and Hölebo hd in Söderman
2 CONC land. Was married to Helena, who was called domina but did not have her own seal.
2 CONT * 2. '''Gregers Magnusson,''' 1318, died trol. 1348, knight, councilor, drots. See tab. 4 .
2 CONT * 2. '''Ingeborg Magnusdotter. Lived in 1331, brought with her estate property in Åkers hd in Södermanland. Still alive in 1358, when she and her children exchanged inheritance for her husband. — Married 4.10 1324 in Stockholm to 
2 CONC Karl Dansson ( Stjärnbjälke ), who is mentioned in 1319, still alive 21.10 1354 but was dead 6.5 1358.'''
2 CONT * 2. '''Margareta Magnusdotter.''' Entered the Sko Cistercian Monastery before 1318. Still alive on 29 May 1328.
2 CONT * 2. '''Kristina Magnusdotter.''' Called "domina Cristina, neptis mea" in her maternal uncle Jedvard Filipsson's will of 1328. Lived in Stockby on Lidingön in 1361. She entered the St. Klara monastery in Stockholm on 21.9.1364 wit
2 CONC h land in Skepptuna sn in Seminghundra hd in Uppland. Was married before 25.3.1327 and probably also before 22.10.1324 to the royal council knight Finvid Nilsson ( Frössviksätten ), who appears in the records no earlier than 5.6.1
2 CONC 298 and, weak in body, made his will on 25.3.1327, when he chose his camp town in Skokloster.
2 CONT * 2. '''Knut Magnusson.''' Mentioned in 1326—1328 as a preacher in Sigtuna.
2 CONT * 2. '''Karl Magnusson,''' 1328—1347. See table 6.
2 CONT * 2. '''Johan Magnusson,''' 1328—1340, knight, lawman (? under-lawman). See tab. 11.
2 CONT * 2. '''Helena Magnusdotter.''' Died no later than 1345. Married no later than 1318 to the royal councilor Karl Orestason ( Färla, Oreste Keldorsson's family ), who is mentioned in 1312 and was still alive in 1335 but was dead in 
2 CONC 1345.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stj%C3%A4rnbj%C3%A4lke For the ennobled but not introduced nobleman Stiernbielke, see Stiernbielke]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bishop Anund Jonsson, who was called Bishop Anund, was bishop in Strängnäs diocese 1275–1291 and stood on Magnus Ladulå's side in the war against his brother Valdemar.  His brother Dan Jonsson (Stjärnbjälke), carried in the coat o
2 CONC f arms three stars on an oblique beam and was a knight and councilor, [2] with a seat in Svälinge. [3] Named in 1295 (sigilant, with a very clear coat of arms seal), [4] in 1297 when he renounces the right to two farms his brother
2 CONC  has bequeathed to the church in Strängnäs, [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke) and Ingeborg Magnusdotter (daughter of Magnus Gregersson who was the grandson of earl Birger), married in 1324 in Stockholm.''' Their daughter Ingegärd Karlsdotter married Ragvald Nilsson (Fargalt) i
2 CONC n 1354, who had a daughter and two sons. Probable son: In 1361 a letter is mentioned in which Gregers Karlsson (Stiernbielke) pledges goods to Ragvald Nilsson.[6] Johan Dansson, canik in Strängnäs, mentioned as brother of Karl Dan
2 CONC sson. [7] In 1385, Mats Gustavsson (sparrow) collected penance from Inge Ingesson (3 stars in column) and Laurens Ingesson (slanted beam coated with three stars) for killing Bård Håkansson (Oxenstierna).[8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1417, on May 9, Inge Ingesson mortgages to Bengt Dansson farms in Ryssby and Böle in Ryssby parish, Norra Möre district.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1599, a Måns Olofsson (Stjärnbjälke) to Ekäng, court eunuch and warlord, is mentioned as the owner of Rösjöholm. Måns was shot during the siege of Kalmar castle on 04/30/1599.[11] Marshal Måns Olofsson (Stiernbielke) was marrie
2 CONC d to Anna Larsdotter Bröms.
2 CONT
2 CONT * The daughter, Margareta Månsdotter (Stjärnbjälke) was married to Göran Armsköld.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Karl+Dansson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_3297&tab=post SDHK no: 3297]
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1324 October 5, Place of issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Dansson gives his wife Ingeborg tomorrow 3 land in Kumla, 20 örtugland in Berga and one öreland in Ingaby. Olof, Archbishop of Uppsala, Knut Jonsson, Erik Valdemarsson, Ulf Gudmarsson, Knut Folkeson, Greger Magnusson and the 
2 CONC issuer seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT A letter of inspection is presented to all. Charles Dansson eternal salvation in the Lord. You have given me, to my dear husband, the underwritten possessions, namely, three marches in the garden. twenty solids in bierghum. and th
2 CONC at one piece of land jn jngaby, by reason of a donation on account of marriages, said vulgarly to be morghongiffh, was released, to be possessed in perpetuity, with such a condition added, that children, if any of us should be pro
2 CONC created by God, should succeed in the said estates, by maternal succession, not paternal, if but the other of us, having no children, happened to be called from this life, the one of us who survived, the estates mentioned let him 
2 CONC retain it, without redemption or demand of any kind. In witness of which, the seals of the venerable father Olaus, Archbishop of Vpsal, and of the noble men, lords, Kanut Jonsson Dapifer, Eric Waldemarsson, Wulfonis Gudmarsson, an
2 CONC d Kanut Folkason, and Gregorij Magnusson, one with my own seal, are attached. Given at Stockholm in the year of the Lord .M.° 300° 244º on the third of the ninth of October.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/3297.pdf Seal]
2 CONT
2 CONT Seal: No. 1, 2, obedydiga fragmenter; No. 3-7 boards; remsorna till alla, utom No. 5, finnas qvar
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Karl+Dansson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_3800&tab=post SDHK no: 3800]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1331 May 20'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Dansson, with the approval of his wife Ingeborg and her brothers, exchanges 9 öresland in Medellenna and Söderllenna to the knight Nils Abjörnsson for a piece of land in Solberga in Teda parish and 2 herbage lands in Bondakyr
2 CONC klinge. Greger Magnusson, Karl Orostoson, Karl Magnusson, Johannes Magnusson and the issuer seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT To all who see this writing, Karolus Dansson, greetings in the lord's sempiternal Noueritis, I have, by the consent of my beloved spouses of Jingburgh, and at the request of the brothers of the same, made an exchange of land with 
2 CONC the noble soldier lord Nicolaus Abiornason in this manner, that I, Charlesus, assign to the same lord Nicolaus and his heirs the new borders of the land in Medhallen and Sudherlen with each and every one of their adjacencies place
2 CONC d near or at a distance to be permanently possessed by right without any encumbrances or exceptions, receiving from the same lord Nicholas for me and my heirs one march of land in the parish of Solberg and two solids of land in th
2 CONC e town of bondakyrlinge under the conditions of all that are expressly stated above Jn the witness of which is the seal of the noble men lords Gregory Magnusson and Karol Orostson of the soldiers, Karol Magnusson and Johannes Magn
2 CONC usson of arms With my and my spouse's presupposed present, I have attached, Given in the year of the Lord 10030330 pentecost
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/3800.pdf Seal]
2 CONT
2 CONT Seal the gates; 3 remsor qvar
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources Original: Or. perg., RA 0101 images, Post-medieval transcripts: Hadorph: E 80, p. 27, No. 13; Örnhielm: Misc. 4:14
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Folkunga%C3%A4ttens_o%C3%A4kta_gren#TAB_3 Folkungaättens oäkta gren]
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Gregersson (son of Gregers, tab. 1). Mentioned on 19.10 1285. Was a squire in 1286 and a knight in 1288. Belonged to King Birger's council apparently already in 1291 and in any case in 1299. Was a lawman in Västmanland in 1
2 CONC 305. Mentioned as alive no later than 13.12 1319. Was dead on 9.1 1326 and was buried with the Dominicans in Sigtuna. Had paternal estate on Arnö in övergrans sn in Håbo hd in Uppland, which he sold to Uppsala cathedral. Owned Bru
2 CONC nnsholm in Näs sn in Åsunda hd in Uppland as well as several landed properties on Ängsö in the same mentioned sn in Yttertjurbo hd in Västmanland, which he exchanged for land in Vallentuna hd in Uppland. In addition, he owned stra
2 CONC w goods in Rasbo, Hagunda, Ulleråkers and Vaksala hd in Uppland. '''Married the first time after 27.9 1282 but before 10.12 1288 to Ragnhild Erlandsdotter who was the daughter of Mr. Erland Israelsson (Finstaätten) and Katarina Jo
2 CONC hansdotter (Ängel), and who had previously been married to Mr. Johan Karlsson (Fånöätten), executed in 1280.''' She drew up her will 10.12 1288 and then chose his camp town at the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. '''Magnus Gregersson
2 CONC  was then, before 4.11 1295, remarried to Ingegärd Filipsdotter, daughter of the knight Filip Finvidsson (Rumbyätten) and a daughter of Karl Tjelvason (Fånöätten).''' As a widow, Ingegärd made her will in 1326 and chose her camp t
2 CONC own with the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. Still alive 16.2 1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peter Magnusson.''' Was underage in 1298 and again in 1302. Was dead on 3.12 1310, when he was buried and his father made his will, in which legacies were assigned to the churches in Fittja in Lagunda hd in Uppland and in 
2 CONC Aspö in Selebo hd in Södermanland, where he apparently owned property. The farm Dalby in Aspö sn in Selebo hd was also determined as a pledge for the legacy. Owned mother land in Frötuna shipyard in Uppland. Inherited from his mat
2 CONC ernal uncle, the canine Karl Erlandsson, land in Färentuna hd in Uppland. Surrendered in 1310 to Sko Kloster for atonement for committed violence land in Frösåkers and Färentuna hd in Uppland, as well as in Svartlösa and Hölebo hd
2 CONC  in Södermanland. Was married to Helena, who was called domina but did not have her own seal.
2 CONT * 2. '''Gregers Magnusson,''' 1318, died trol. 1348, knight, councillor, drots. See tab. 4.
2 CONT * 2. '''Ingeborg Magnusdotter.''' Lived in 1331, brought in the estate goods in Åkers hd in Södermanland. Still alive in 1358, when she and the children passed on the inheritance to the husband. — Married on 4 October 1324 in Stoc
2 CONC kholm to Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke), who is mentioned in 1319, was still alive on 21 October 1354 but died on 6 May 1358.
2 CONT * 2. '''Margareta Magnusdotter.''' Entered Sko Cistercian monastery before 1318. Still alive 29.5 1328.
2 CONT * 2. '''Kristina Magnusdotter.''' Called "domina Cristina, neptis mea", in her maternal uncle Jedvard Filipsson's will in 1328. Lived in 1361 in Stockby on Lidingön. On 21.9 1364 she entered St. Klara monastery in Stockholm with l
2 CONC and in Skepptuna sn in Seminghundra hd in Uppland. Was before 25.3 1327 and probably also before 22.10 1324 married to the Riksdag knight Finvid Nilsson (Frössviksätten), who appears in the records no earlier than 5.6 1298 and, we
2 CONC ak in body, made his will 25.3 1327, when he chose his camp town in Skokloster.
2 CONT * 2. '''Knut Magnusson.''' Mentioned 1326-1328 as preacher brother in Sigtuna.
2 CONT * 2. '''Karl Magnusson,''' 1328—1347. See tab. 6.
2 CONT * 2. '''Johan Magnusson,''' 1328—1340, knight, lawman (? subordinate). See tab. 11.
2 CONT * 2. '''Helena Magnusdotter.''' Died no later than 1345. Married no later than 1318 to Riksrad Karl Orestason (Färla, Oreste Keldorsson's family), who is mentioned in 1312 and was still alive in 1335 but was dead in 1345.
2 CONT
2 CONT
