1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Halsten Johansson Halv Lilja=
2 CONT
2 CONT =PLEASE DON’T DISCONNECT AND GO OF THE FAMILY TREE IN WIKIPEDIA.  THE DATES & FAMILY LINE ARE INCORRECT.  WE HAVE HAD TO CORRECT THIS LINE MULTIPLE OF TIMES! =  
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Johan Halstensson Halv Lilja
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Grandfather Riddare Halsten Petersson Halv Lilja was born about 1300. He passed away on March 1, 1358.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Foremost in Småland's Njudung, 1329 - 1357/58, appears the Knight (and bailiff) Halsten Petersson, he belonged to the old Høgfrälse family (Halv Lilja) and shows in his coat of arms a brisire of a lily, a change of a sprung Lilje 
2 CONC - coat of arms. This points to the occurrence of an old lily - leading family in Njudung, decided in the areas around Halleberg and Hundeberg, along the Gøta river. J.Raneke certainly misreads Halstens' coat of arms as a transvers
2 CONC ally divided Lilja, because Halstens' coat of arms is found on a famous folding table in Luneburg in Germany and shows a Kluven Halv Lilja (in Ginbalk). (Lily is in Yellow on Red field.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1355, Sofi mentions a "Halsten i Tracksta" and on 24 February 1358 we find Halsten Thrægsta, as a resident of Vadsbro. (Halsten died between 24 February 1358 - and 29 September 1358). From 18 May 1362 to 7 May. In 1401 we find 
2 CONC a Peter in Tracksta, mentioned 8 times, mostly as a regular.
2 CONT
2 CONT The farms Fors and Åsbräcka in the parish of Flundra here and were only a few miles from the church in Gårdhem, where the Liljestenene are, and to which Mrs. Lucias Matsdatter's sister Bengta Matsdatter gave gifts in her will in 1
2 CONC 338, presumably because there were old family ties between the farms and the families in Gardhem and the farms and families in Flundre hereafter. The close ties are particularly shown by Halsten Peterson's brother (half-brother?) 
2 CONC Arvid Peterson who carried a Sparrow in his weapon. In the work itself, it can be ascertained that the lily-carrying Halsten Peterson was the daughter's son of the knight Abjørn (Asbjørn ?) Sparre and Mrs. Lucia Matsdatter, as wel
2 CONC l as presumably the brother Arvid Peterson Sparre. This is proven by the fact that Abjørn Sparre and Lucia Matsdatter's daughter Margareta Abjørnsdatter, when she sells her share in the farm Berg in Fråstad in 1341 (DS.3591), ment
2 CONC ions Halsten Peterson as her blood relative, it is further proven by Margareta's will from 1342 ( DS.3614) in which she directly mentions him as her Sororio. That is, his sister's son. Thus, Halsten belonged to Peterson, as did hi
2 CONC s brother (Abjørn) Aberno (Ant. error for Arvid). on the mother's side, the Abjørnske Sparre family in Flundre here. The knight Abjørn Sparre and Lucia Madsdatter had the children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''Margareta Abjørnsdatter Sparre (mentioned 1341) (DS.3591) married to Johan Soneson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''Bengt Abjörnsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. '''Gustav Abjörnsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. '''Elena Abjörnsdotter fift with Knut Sigvidsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''Ingrid Abjørnsdotter Sparre''' married 2nd to (Norwegian) Håkan Bårdson married 1st to Peter (Halv lilja), from Njudung, this Peter is believed to have carried the same weapon as (Sønnen) Halsten Petersson. Here a connection
2 CONC  appears between the Lilje family and one of the old Abjørn Sparre family, which consisted of the family Sparre of Tofta, the Abjørn Spar family, in Flundra here. and Abjørn Ulfsson Sparreætt from Finnveden. There is in particular
2 CONC  a letter dated 21 Sept. 1340 that points out Ingrid Abjørnsdatter Sparre as the mother of Knight Halsten Petersson, in which a man named Olof Gren who, according to the Västergøta law, gave Halsten Petersson all the estates in Fr
2 CONC åstad as Håkan Bårdson, s wife Ingrid Abjørnsdatter had inherited from her aunt Bengta Madsdatter. This indicates that it is Halsten Petersson who takes over the inheritance from his mother. Olof Gren was presumably identical to t
2 CONC he Oluf Ebbeson (Sparre) who appears in a letter dated Upplanda at Kinnekulla on 9 April 1367 and who, according to a letter 4 October 1366, was the brother of Erengisle Ebbeson's father, Ebbe Gren (Sparre). These are closely rela
2 CONC ted to the family called Unnesønnenes Sparre Ætt, which in turn is close to Jöns Abjørnsson's Sparre over sea leaf (so the Forstena family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Halsten Petersson is mentioned in 1355, and was the confidant of King Magnus Erikson of Sweden (born 1316 - 1374), and King Magnus gives Halsten, the farm Gäddgøl, Svarthøfdaryd, Ulvsmåla, Eringsboda and Broddamåla (25 
2 CONC April 1338). But he participated in (King) Erik Magnusson's rebellion against his father, and is mentioned among Erik's 5 pledges in 1357. Halsten Petersson Halv Lilja (c.1300? - 1358) was married to Märta (also called Margreta) K
2 CONC nutsdatter (with armsTre Rosor) . Named Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1st? '''Peter Halstensson'''  (ca.1330? - ), is probably the Peter mentioned from and on in Tracksta 18 May to 7 May 1401, most often as fasting. Land in Fyrby in Blacksta parish and Vik in Vadsbro parish (Sweden) is said to be 
2 CONC his right Byrd (Odel?).
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2. '''Håkon Halstensson''' ca.1333? - ), mentioned 5 March 1377 in Sundby in Forsa parish, and 1385, married to Bengta Siggesdatter, daughter of Sigge Magnusson mentioned 1339 (in connection with Tracksta?).
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3. '''Knut Halstensson''' ca.1335? - )
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4. '''Cecilia Halstensdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * ?5. '''a Märta Halstensdotter is mentioned in 1383, in connection with Bo Jonson (Hyltinge parish, Sweden.)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters: 5 March 1377, Sudby in Forsa Parish. Håkon Halstensson drafts a letter on the occasion of the land swap that Mr. Lidinvard Haraldsson on behalf of the executor was made in 
2 CONC Forsa with the executor's mother Mrs. Märta Knutsdotter and his brother (=Knut) in the presence of Bishop Tomas in Växö, Johan Gregersson, and Mr. Peter in By, concerning both the fathers, the mothers, and the mother's gift. The e
2 CONC xecutor (Håkan Halstensson) exchanges the previously unexchanged estate with his mother and his brother Knut Halstensson in such a way that he leaves to them his entire share (ægondel) in Fornåsa in Boberg hereafter in return for 
2 CONC the executor seals together with the Knights Ragnvald Magnusson and Ingvald Anundsson as well as Mr. Jacob in Forsa..
2 CONT
2 CONT Halsten Petersson's family, also called Half Lily, is a contemporary conventional name for a Swedish medieval squire family that took the name from the progenitor, knight and bailiff Halsten Petersson . The family dies out (on the
2 CONC  direct male line) before Swedens Ridderhus was founded in 1625 which is why it was never introduced there as a nobility. Halsten had a brother (half brother) Arvid Petersson who carrieda Spar (Sparre) in his coat of arms. In 1336
2 CONC  and 1338 he was given goods and thanks for faithful serviceby the king Magnus Eriksson . But he participated in King Erik Magnusson's rebellion against his father, and is mentioned among Eriks five pledges in 1357. He is stated t
2 CONC o be died betveen 24 of Febrary and 29 of Sept.1358 (some say March1.1358, but i have not seen any sources for this). Wnen Halsten Petersson actally was born is unknown, but based on the years mentioned of his childtrens living, h
2 CONC e may well have been born around year 1300 , plus- minus?. He was married to Märta (also called Margreta) Knutsdaughter (coat of arms Three Rosor (Tre Rosor). (born about !300/10?). A daughter of Knut (Tre Rosor), married to Krist
2 CONC ina Bengtsdaughter (Lejon) in Hanastrøm , who was a daughter of the lawman in Västergøtland (in Sweden) Bengt Hafridsson (Lejon).
2 CONT
2 CONT Halsten Peterssons coat of arms is depicted on a klaffbord in Luneburg (in Germany) and shows a half Lily, in Ginbalk, a fragmented shield with the upper field (not a split) . Jan Raneke is therefore incorrect when he said it is a
2 CONC  half lily lying on the division.
2 CONT
2 CONT
