1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sune Jonsson (Bååt)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jon Pedersson (Bååt) and Ingeborg Eriksdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr: 3723'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Date: 1330 July 8'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Content'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '' 'Sune Jonsson' '', Karl Bengtsson, '' 'Peter Johansson' '', Ernelius Kettilbjörnsson, Joar Birgersson, Algot by Gillerhälla attest to how the dispute between Algot by Gillerhälla and Hemming Tanne concerning Johan Ragvaldsson, 
2 CONC Kettilögas and Erina's estate was resolved thus, to report Algot on behalf of his wife Astrid shall keep the goods in Riseberga and Sjösäter, which she received from Johan Ragvaldsson and Bildstens meadow, and Hemming the goods in
2 CONC  Söderby, which Erina gave him and the goods in Bjärestad, Ingelstad and Baggetorp as he bought from Kettilög. The inheritance rights to Johan Ragvaldsson's and his sister Ragnhild's estate are determined.
2 CONT The issuers seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SEAL'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The seal: N: o 1, Sune Jonssons (boat)
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument?namn=pdf/3723.pdf&serverId=26
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Baat Adelsvapen==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Batt Adelsvapen''' - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/B%C3%A5%C3%A5t_nr_3#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT Sune Jonsson (son of Jon, Tab. 1). Was knight 1315-09-09 when he participated in the so-called change of commands between the dukes Erik and Valdemar, and the council of 1313-07-28. Participated in Skara Association 1322-07-20. Va
2 CONC r was attached to Kalmar castle on 1329-02-02 and the layman in Tiohärad's lawsuit 1337-01-13, when he pledged all his goods in Vedbo hardened to security for 200 marks, which he borrowed from Bishop Karl in Linköping. Also owned 
2 CONC property in Alsheda in Njudung. Deceased before 1339-10-12. He, like brother Peter Jonsson, played a prominent role in the recovery of Viborg in 1321 and participated in Skåne's possession. 1332. '''Married  (1): o Karin Henriksdo
2 CONC tter, daughter of the knight Henrik Glysing.''' '''Married 2: o with Helga Bengtsdotter (winged arrow), in her 1st marriage.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margaret Sunesdotter;'''  She donated all her estate in Kläckeberga parish to Kalmar nunnery in 1360-12-21 and was still living 1362-02-05, when she was living at Fogelvik, which she seems to have owned. Married before 1337-0
2 CONC 1-13 with the knight and the National Council, the lawman in Tiohärad's court case Ulf Abiörnsson ( Sparre av Tofta ) in his 2nd marriage (married 1st with Christina Sigmundsdotter, daughter of Sigmund Keldorsson), dead before 135
2 CONC 0-03- 07th
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Sunesdotter''', dead before 1348. Married before 1339-10-12 with the knight and the Swedish Nils Turesson ( Bielke ) in his 1st marriage, died in 1364.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Erengisle Sunesson,''' Be with the Western Gothic man Knut Magnusson King Magnus Eriksson accordingly on his sailing trip to Namur 1334; knights are mentioned for the first time Oct 25 1344 and the Swedish National Council 4 
2 CONC Aug. 1350; attended the men's day in Jönköping 1351; acquired the title of Earl of the Orkney Islands in May 1353; was governor of Sevede, heralded June 19, 1362. Married 1) to Margaret ...; 2) with Annot (Agneta, Agnes), † before
2 CONC  21 Dec. 1360, probably daughter of Orkneyjar Malise of Stratherne; 3) before Oct. 20. 1377 with Ingeborg Magnusdotter (lion), † 1390 (buried June 28), daughter of the knight Magnus Gudmarsson ( Ulvåsaätten ) and widow of the nati
2 CONC onal council Bengt Turesson ( Bielke ).
2 CONT * ''''Unknown daughter'''  Married to the National Council and the Governor of Östergötland Nils Jonsson (seven-star), which in two letters 1360-12-21 is called "may" by Erengisle Sunesson and his sister Margareta.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
