1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * In Danish: http://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofia_af_Minsk   
2 CONT
2 CONT ***  In English: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_of_Minsk
2 CONT
2 CONT ****  http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00029924&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ****  http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I9378&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia Queen Consort Of Denmark Vladimirovna    ***
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sofia af Minsk''' (Sofija Vladimirovna eller Sofia Volodarsdatter) - var dronning af Danmark. Gift 23. oktober 1157 med kong Valdemar den Store af Danmark. [http://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofia_af_Minsk Wikipedia DA]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''София Владимировна''' - княжна минская, королева датская. [http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%BE%D1%84%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BD%D0%B0 Wikipedia RU]
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as Sophie von Minsk, Sophie av Halicz and Sophie Princess of Russia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_of_Minsk and in Danish:  http://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofia_af_Minsk Sophia of Minsk (or Sophia of Polotsk) (ca. 11
2 CONC 40 – 5 May 1198) was a Danish mediaeval queen consort as the spouse of King Valdemar I of Denmark, and later a landgravine of Thuringia. Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia was the daughter of Richeza of Poland, Dowager Queen of Sweden, from her marriage to a man called "Valador" King in Poloni Land. Several speculations have been put forward as to exactly who her father was, but his identity 
2 CONC is still uncertain. It is guessed[who?] to have been Prince Volodar of Minsk or Prince Vladimir of Halicz. Most probably it was Volodar (Valadar in Belarusian) of Minsk, who united the principalities of Minsk, Polotsk, and Hrodna 
2 CONC under his rule, and had military interests in the Baltic region (for example, his military campaign in Northern Poland in 1159).[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia was the half-sister of Canute V of Denmark. After her mother's marriage to the Swedish king, she followed her to Sweden and was raised at the Swedish court. She was betrothed to Valdemar in 1154 as a form of alliance betwee
2 CONC n Denmark and Sweden. As she had no property in Denmark, she was promised 1/8 of Canute's estates. She left Sweden and arrived in Denmark at the time of the engagement (1154), but as she was not considered old enough to marry, she
2 CONC  was given to the custody of a woman named Bodil. She was married to Valdemar in Viborg in 1157, three years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia is described as beautiful, dominant and cruel. According to legend,[which?] she murdered Valdemar's mistress Tove and injured his sister Kirsten, but this is not confirmed. She was widowed in 1182. Sophia received a proposa
2 CONC l from, and married, Louis III, Landgrave of Thuringia in about 1184, and was escorted to the border by her son and a grand entourage. She was repudiated in 1190 and returned to Denmark. [edit] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia married Valdemar I of Denmark (c 1131–1182), and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * King Canute VI of Denmark (1163–1202)
2 CONT     * King Valdemar II of Denmark (1170–1241)
2 CONT     * Sophia (1159 –1208), married Siegfried III, Count of Orlamünde
2 CONT     * Margaret and Maria, nuns at Roskilde
2 CONT     * Richeza of Denmark (died 1220), married King Eric X of Sweden
2 CONT     * Helena (died 1233), married William, Duke of Brunswick-Luneburg
2 CONT     * Ingeborg (1175–1236), married King Philip II of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia of Minsk Queen consort of Danmark Tenure 	1157–1182 Spouse 	Valdemar I of Denmark Issue Canute VI of Denmark Valdemar II of Denmark Richeza, Queen of Sweden Ingeborg, Queen of France more Dynasty 	Rurikid? Father 	Volodar o
2 CONC f Minsk Mother 	Richeza of Poland Born 	1138/41 Died 	5 May 1198 Burial 	St. Bendt's Church
2 CONT
2 CONT Dronning Sofie, født 1140, datter af fyrst Vladimir af Novgorod og prinsesse Richiza. Ægteskabet med Valdemar blev indgået i Viborg den 23 oktober 1157. Efter Valdemars død i 1182 giftede enkedronningen sig med landsgreve Ludvig a
2 CONC f Thuringen, men blev efter kort tid skilt og sendt tilbage til Danmark. Død 5 maj 1198. Gravsat i Ringsted ved Valdemars side.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie var datter til den polske hertugdatteren Richiza (Richeza, Ryksa, Rixa) Boleslawsdatter i hennes annet ekteskap med fyrsten Vladimir (Valedar, Volodar). Det er omstritt hvem denne Vladimir var, men i sin stamtavle over de d
2 CONC anske konger kaller Abbed Vilhelm [ca. 1125-1203] Sophies far <Valedar, russernes konge>.
2 CONT
2 CONT I sitt første ekteskap med Magnus, sønn til kong Niels I Svendsson den Gamle av Danmark, fikk Richiza sønnen Knud, senere Knud Magnusson III av Danmark. Knud lot seg hylde som konge på Jylland og Fyn, mens Svend III Grathe var han
2 CONC s medkonge på Sjælland. Stridigheter mellom de to kulminerte ved blodgildet i Roskilde 1157 hvor Knud ble myrdet. Richiza giftet seg en tredje gang med kong Sverker I den Eldre av Sverige, og fikk med ham sønnen Bulislaw (Boleslaw
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Knud og Sophie var altså halvsøsken.
2 CONT
2 CONT Da Valdemar og Knud III Magnusson hadde nærmet seg hverandre, ble det i 1154 avtalt ekteskap mellom Sophie og Valdemar. Da Sophie selv ikke eide gods i Danmark, lovet Knud å utstyre henne med en tredjedel av sin egen farsarv. Alle
2 CONC rede før Valdemars endelige seier på Grathehede ble deres bryllup feiret i Viborg i 1157.
2 CONT
2 CONT Svend Aggesen [ca. 1130 - ca. 1185] berømmer Sophie for hennes store skjønnhet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Valdemar og Sophie hadde følgende barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie, gift med greve Siegfried III av Orlamünde, død ca. 1210.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1163: Knud IV av Danmark, gift med Gertrude av Bayern, død 1202.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1170: Valdemar II Sejr av Danmark, gift med Berengaria av Portugal, død 1241.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richiza, gift med kong Erik Knutsson av Sverige, død 1220.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg, gift med kong Filip II August av Frankrike, død 1236.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helene, gift med hertug Wilhelm av Lüneburg, død 1233.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dertil to døtre som gikk i kloster og som vi ikke sikkert kjenner navnene til.
2 CONT
2 CONT En av disse sistnevnte døtre ble forlovet med en sønn til keiser Frederik Barbarossa på et tidspunkt da Valdemar søkte samarbeide med keiseren. Etter Valdemars død fortsatte Knud IV denne politikk, idet han lot sin mor gifte seg m
2 CONC ed keiserens betrodde mann, greve Ludvig III av Thüringen. Senere, da forholdet mellom konge og keiser ble mer spent, ble såvel Sophie som hennes datter forstøtt av sine ektemenn og sendt tilbake til Danmark. Sophie skal ha blitt 
2 CONC meget bitter av denne behandling ifølge Arnold av Lübeck som skrev <Chronica Slavorum> 1172-1209 og døde i 1211 eller 1214. De danske kilder omtaler ikke denne pinlige episode.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie døde 05.05.1198 og ble begravet i Ringsted. 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Politiken's Danmarks Historie, Bind 3 (1969), side 62, 200, 202, 211, 275, 324, 408. Dansk Biografisk Leksikon, Bind 11 (1937), side 190, Bind 22 (1942), side 294-295, Bind 25 (1943), side 23. Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 5
2 CONC 84. Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 44, 88. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Dronning af Danmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie har været en stærk og selvbevidst personlighed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hun prises for sin skønhed af Sven Aggesen, som selv har set hende
2 CONT
2 CONT Giftede sig med Ludwig straks efter Valdemars død, kort tid efter skilt
2 CONT
2 CONT og sendt tilbage til Danmark. Begravet ved siden af Valdemar i Ringsted
2 CONT
2 CONT I folkeviserne er hun blevet den skinsyge dronning der lader Valdemars
2 CONT
2 CONT frille Tove brænde i badstuen.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Kilde: Dahl & Engelstoft: Dansk Biografisk Håndleksikon. 1920-26)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Kilde: Salmonsens Konversations Leksikon, 2' udg. 1915-1930)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia of Minsk or Sophie of Polotzk (born around 1140, possibly between 1138 and 1141-1198), was a Danish mediavel queen, Queen consort of King Valdemar I of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT She was half-sister of Canute V of Denmark and daughter of Dowager Queen Rikissa of Sweden from her marriage with a father called "Valador" King in Poloni Lands. Several speculations have been put forward as to exactly who her fat
2 CONC her was, but his identity is still uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a widow, Sofia married Louis III, Landgrave of Thuringia in about 1184, but was repudiated very soon after the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children and family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia married Valdemar I of Denmark (c 1131-1182), and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT King Canute VI of Denmark (1163-1202) 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar II of Denmark (1170-1241) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie, (1159 –1208), married Siegfried III, Count of Orlamünde 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta and Maria, nuns at Roskilde 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rikissa of Denmark (died 1220), married King Eric X of Sweden 
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen (died 1233), married William, Duke of Brunswick-Luneburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg (1175-1236), married King Philip II of France 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sophie OF DENMARK b: 1159
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Waldemar II OF DENMARK
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Richiza OF DENMARK
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Estrid Waldemarsdatter OF DENMARK
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Helena OF DENMARK
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia was the daughter of Dowager Queen Rikissa of Sweden from her marriage with to a man called "Valador" King in Poloni Land. Several speculations have been put forward as to exactly who her father was, but his identity is stil
2 CONC l uncertain; he is guessed[who?] to have been Prince Volodar of Minsk or Prince Vladimir of Halicz. Most probably it was Volodar (Valadar in Belarusian) of Minsk who united principalities of Minsk, Polotsk, and Hrodna under his ru
2 CONC le, and had military interests in the Baltics region (for example, his military campaign in Northern Poland in 1159).[citation needed] Sophia was the half-sister of Canute V of Denmark. She was bethrothed in 1154, and married in 1
2 CONC 157 to Valdemar.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is described as beautiful but cruel in the legends,[which?] where she murdered Valdemar's mistress Tove, and injured his sister Kirsten, but this is not confirmed. As a widow, Sofia married Louis III, Landgrave of Thuringia in
2 CONC  about 1184, but was repudiated very soon after the marriage, and returned to Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noteringar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Syster till kung Knut II Magnusson 
2 CONT
