1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingevald Folkesson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Folke "Filbyter" and Bertrande Jorgrimmesdotter De Monfort 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://uddautflykter.se/guide/ostergotland/bjalbo-runstenar-og-64-og-66/ Bjälbo Runestones ÖG 64 & ÖG 66]
2 CONT
2 CONT front of Bjälbo church stand two large runestones, both of which give fragmentary clues to an ancient time hidden in the mists of time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Östergötland's runic inscriptions 64 are called the Bjälbostenen and are the oldest written source that mentions guilds, the medieval associations that are the model for today's associations.
2 CONT The first known guild in nearby Skänninge is mentioned in 1370 when the All Saints Guild buys a property in the town, which was probably a religious association. The purpose of the guild mentioned on the Bjälbostenen is, however, 
2 CONC unknown. The rune stone is over three meters high and tells through its runes that:
2 CONT "Brave men erected this stone after Grep, his guild brother, Judde's son. Love carved these runes.”
2 CONT Next to it is also the rune stone ÖG 66, which is also historically interesting as it tells that it was erected by Birger Jarl's ancestor Ingevald Folkesson, the son of Bjälboätten's ancestor Folke Filbyter. The four-meter-high ru
2 CONC nestone tells that:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ingevald raised this stone after Styvjald, his brother, an excellent youth, son of Spialbode for the family, but I completed it."
2 CONT
2 CONT Both monumental runestones are stops on a runestone safari around Mjölby's plain landscape and are often combined with a visit to the medieval defense tower and the memorial stone for Birger Jarl.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://reader.digitale-sammlungen.de/en/fs1/object/display/bsb10328239_00031.html
2 CONT * http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingevald_Folkesson
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Folkunga%C3%A4tten
2 CONT
