1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Christina Ingesdotter of Sweden==
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cristina_Ingesdotter_de_Suecia
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina Ingesdotter of Sweden in her deathbed, with her husband (Mstislav I) next to her; Death of Daniil Yureviski; March of courtesans and bishops. Added by Janet Milburn 2/25/18 as the one that
2 CONT had been used was Queen Margaret, another of my ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Christina Ingesdotter of Sweden (Swedish: Kristina Ingesdotter; 11th century – d. 18 January 1122) was a Swedish princess and, by marriage, a princess of Veliky Novgorod, Rostov and Belgorod, spouse of Grand Prince Mstisl
2 CONC av I of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina was the daughter of King Inge the Elder of Sweden and queen Helena. She was married to Mstislav in 1095, who was prince of Veliky Novgorod, Rostov and Belgorod during their marriage, thereby giving her the equivalent tit
2 CONC les. Three years after her death in 1122, her spouse became Grand Prince of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Issue===
2 CONT
2 CONT # Ingeborg of Kiev, married Canute Lavard of Jutland, and was mother to Valdemar I of Denmark
2 CONT # Malmfred, married (1) Sigurd I of Norway; (2) Eric II of Denmark
2 CONT # Eupraxia, married Alexius Comnenus, son of John II Comnenus
2 CONT # Vsevolod of Novgorod and Pskov
2 CONT # Maria, married Vsevolod II of Kiev
2 CONT # Iziaslav II of Kiev
2 CONT # Rostislav of Kiev
2 CONT # Sviatopolk of Pskov
2 CONT # Rogneda, married Yaroslav of Volinya
2 CONT # Xenia, married Briachislav of Izyaslawl
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 18 JAN 1121/22
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links===
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00027051&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Христина Ингесдоттер (умерла 18 января 1122) — шведская принцесса, первая жена Мстислава I Владимировича Великого, князя новгородского, потом (уже после её смерти) великого князя киевского, дочь короля Швеции Инге Стенкильсона из 
2 CONC династии Стенкилей и Хелены, сестры шведского короля Блот-Свена.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
