2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1383 March 17, Place of issue: Nykoping''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Content'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight Nils Gädda and his wife Kristina Magnusdotter exchange to the lord Bo Jonsson Sundbyholm in Sundby etc. in Bälinge parish (Röne district), Sulta, Sörby etc. in Tystberga parish (Rönö district), Kvarnby etc. in Västerljung p
2 CONC arish (Hölebo district) in exchange for the estates he received from Ragvald Nilsson (Fargalt) and his wife Ingrid Karlsdotter (Stjärnbalk) and from Lars Ragvaldsson and his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources: Original:'''  or. perg. RA 0101(Engestr. collection)  pictures, Post-medieval copies:  (around 1605) Sturannas Copiebok p. 103, LUB, Dlg, Sture 2.: B 19 a no. 7, RA 0107.03 (Note by Hog. Bielke: Wiss Copia...huffueh 
2 CONC breffuith hos frue Margareta på Broo".) Post-medieval regest/notice:  Reg. Vretstorp E 9, ULA (Photo DK), (Excerpt) De la Gardiska Archivet 3, p. 129 f., Printed register List of a collection of perfbrefs in ...von Engeström's lib
2 CONC rary (1819), p. 13 (no. 28).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Literature and commentary'''
2 CONT * See G. Carlsson, PHT 1951, p. 4 note 4. - G. Lundberg, Bälinge socken under medeltiden, 1976, p. 30 f. nusv. translation p. 69 ff. On the back of the letter Margareta Grip's signature. Cf. L. Sjödin in MRA 1939, p. 115 note 2.; 
2 CONC Regarding Sundboholm, see A.-C. Mattisson, Medieval Nordic castle and manor names in -holm (1986), pp. 74 f. Regarding Örboholm, see A.-C. Mattisson, Medieval Nordic castle and manor names in -holm (1986), pp. 76 ff.
