2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Bårdsson was born about 1270?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nothing is known about Håkan Bårdsson's origin, it is said that he was Norwegian, but no source has been found for this. Håkan Bårdsson is mentioned as married to Ingrid Abjörnsdotter (Sparre), and they had a son Bård Håkansson, w
2 CONC ho was killed by his relative (cousin) Mats Gustavsson (Sparre) (Son of Ingrid's brother Gustav Abjörnsson). Håkan Bårdsson's wife Ingrid held in 1340 hereditary land in Frastaha (DS 3420), which she had inherited from her "Auuncu
2 CONC la" Bengta (Matsdotter) along with her sisters Margareta Abjörnsdotter, Elena Abjörnsdotter, who were sisters of Gustav and Bengt Abjörnsson (Sparre). Ingrid Abjörnsdotter (Sparre) was married for the first time to a Peter, and al
2 CONC l the aforementioned hereditary estates in Frastadha were sold by their owners to Halsten Petersson, whom Margareta Abjörnsdotter calls "consanguineus" (DS 3597). (DS 3591) The information in this letter can be compiled with the f
2 CONC act that in her will of 1341 (DS 3614) she speaks of her "Sororius" Halsten and his brother Abjörn (which is probably a misspelling for Arvid). This Halsten Petersson (Half Lily, in Ginbalk, not a half lily lying along the side of
2 CONC  the shield, but a half lily without a stem, in the upper field of the shield), who was the son of Ingrid and Peter, was married to Märta Knutsdotter (Tre Rosor). He died in 1358. Halsten Peterson acquired another part in Frastadu
2 CONC m in 1350 (Ds 4542 and 4543).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hans Gillingstam: Attarna Öxenstierna och Vasa Under Medeltiden - Släkthistoriska Studier (1952)
