2 CONT
2 CONT 242242 Övergrans parish In the change of inheritance after Gustav I, Ekolsund fell to Johan III, and from 1569 Ekolsund was granted to Duchess Sofia and her son, Duke Gustav (AL 1 p. 179). The following regents issue letters at Ek
2 CONC olsund: Erik & Valdemar 1307 (DS 1543, DS 1544). Gustav I (large number of letters) (1529 GR 6 p 338, 1558 GR 28 p 486) Dukes Erik and Valdemar are on E, where they issue letters of protection for Sko monastery and for the convent
2 CONC ion in Sigtuna (DS 1543, DS 1544) '''is Didrik in E fasting at the county council (DS 2484) celebrates Guttorm Toresson(split shield) and his wife Inga Gregersdotter (Malsta family) their wedding at E''' (DS 3276) Katarina Magnusd
2 CONC otter inherits E from her father Magnus Knutsson (Aspenäs family) (DS 7815) Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta) and Bo Jonsson (Grip) that Finvid Finvidsson (Frössviks family), on behalf of his wife Katarina Magnusdotter, received E an
2 CONC d all goods in Uppsala diocese in the inheritance of Katarina's father Magnus Knutsson (Aspenäs family) (DS X 252) gives Bengt Jönsson (Oxenstierna ) 8:0 in E and in the estates that are adjacent tomorrow gift to his wife Kristina
2 CONC  Kristiernsdotter (Vasa) (SD 2292) goes to E with underlying estates Archbishop Jöns Bengtsson (Oxenstierna) in the event of succession between him and his brothers after their father Bengt Jönsson (OxS E 522, GiOV p 332 f) bequea
2 CONC ths Kristina Davidsdotter (Oxenstierna), with her daughter Märta's consent,farm E to her husband Bengt Arentsson (Ulv) for his lifetime (U 269 as 26, GiOV p 494 f) (around) Jöran Åkesson (Tott) changes E away to Gustav I (AH p 28 
2 CONC f, GR 14 p 12, ÄSF I:3 p 285) E is mentioned among the farms that will supply food to Stockholm Palace in connection with the unrest in the country (GR 14 p 283 ff) see Arnö.
2 CONT
