1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Knut Arvidsson, till Torpa =
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Arvid Jönsson (Sparre över Stjärna) and Ingegärd Petersdotter  (ej Prika, det är en annan person)
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/161183967/knut-arvidsson-drake_af_intorp_sparre_ver_stj_rna_ '''Find a Grave Memorial for Knut Arvidsson Drake af Intorp (sparre över stjärna)''']
2 CONT *  [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82#TAB_3 '''Knut Arvidsson, till Torpa'''] i Länghems socken, Älvsborgs län.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Married: 1439 with [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000005035483019?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000174643765890 '''Kerstin Bengtsdotter (Compan),'''] Widow lived 1459, daughter of the Hallingian Archer Bengt Turess
2 CONC on ( Companion , Spider Over Leaf) 
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000005035483019&photo_id=6000000174643765890&position=0  (2) '''Märta Gunnarsdotter ( Gylta ).''']  Daughter of Gunnar Nilsson Gylta, till Påtorp and Märta
2 CONC  Olofsdotter Oxehufvud, till Påtorp till Hellerup.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Arvid Knutsson'''. National Council and Teamman. Death 1497. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Märta Knutsdotter.''' married in 1487 with the chieftain Brother Buth in his 2nd marriage (1: o m. Margareta Mårtensdotter, daughter of Mårten Svensson), lived yet 1507.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Knutsdotter,''' (Also called Ingegärd) Married to the gunman Håkan Karlsson Tun .
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Brita Knutsdotter.,''' married to Nils (? Halvardsson) ( wasting under half star ).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Karin Knutsdotter,''' dead childless
2 CONT
2 CONT [Eara; SoH: 1955 s290; SoH: 1959 sl73ff; SoH: 1969 s232ff; ASF: In s216]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/17620#/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/17618 Dragon, Relatives]
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake, savior families from Småland and Östergötland. Mainly in Småland appear during the late Middle Ages two low-saved families, in the literature called Sunnerbo-Drakarna and Västbo - Drakarna . The former included a. Magnus Bi
2 CONC rgersson Drake(still living 1465, was d. 1474) to Kalvnäs in Högsby sn (Kalm.), bailiff at Stäkeborg 1427, district chief in Aspeland and Sevede 1448 (cf. Svea Court of Appeal Liber causarum 60, no. 6, National Archives), Another 
2 CONC branch owned from the end of the 14th century to into the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the family, which was disputed already in an inheritance process in 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactorily inve
2 CONC stigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this family would possibly descend the noble family, which was introduced in 1646 and then became called Drake af Torp and Hamra (proba
2 CONC bly extinct in 1709); the baptismal name Christer used in the latter generation, however, rather indicates kinship with Västboätten. Colonel Johan Christersson Drake af Torp and Hamra belonged to the family, who fell in the battle
2 CONC  of Landskrona in 1677. Among his children are the lieutenant colonel, Fredrik Drake (b. 1660), who fell in the battle of Pultava in 1709 and is mentioned in Heidenstam's short story »Poltava» in »Karolinerna», and Sophia Drake (d
2 CONC . 1741 ), gm Lieutenant Colonel Jon Stålhammar and in literature known as the one sung by Snoilsky in «Swedish pictures» «Mrs. at Salshult». - Västbo-Drakarnas (weapon: flying dragon) ancestor Kristiern Drake is said to have marri
2 CONC ed Margareta Krumme, widow of the district chief Olof Jönsson (older Stenbocksätten). The son Olof (Kristersson) Drake was for a long time and still in 1518 district chief in Västbo. His grandson in the equestrian master Olof Nils
2 CONC son Drake (d. 1590) - on the father of the family (coat of arms: chevron over star) that still survives in the noble family Capricorn - took the name D., and the family branch introduced in 1625 and extinct in 1635, is known as Dr
2 CONC ake af Intorp . About Olof Nilsson's father's cousin ,, Councilor Arvid Knutsson ;, (d. 1497) and his son the gunsmith and district chief Olof Arvidsson (d. 1508), who took up the maiden weapon (Capricorn), see Capricorn. Olof Kri
2 CONC stersson D: son (Olof Nilsson D: uncle) Arvid Olofsson Drake (d. After 1532), bailiff in Allbo and östbo, was the father of Märta Arvidsdotter, g. Around 1550 m. Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand); cf. Hand , relatives. Their son
2 CONC  the governor Arvid Knutsson Drake (d. Trol. 1618) took the mother's name and became the ancestor of the family Drake af Hagelsrum, see this.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Hildebrand.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://daten.digitale-sammlungen.de/~db/bsb00000600/images/index.html?seite=969&fip=193.174.98.30
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elgenstierna, Gustaf ,: The introduced Swedish noble genealogy Drake af Intorp Tab 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Knut Arvidsson (son of Arvid Jönsson, Tab. 2), to Torpa in Länghems parish, Älvsborg county. Called Arms 1438-12-14. Chief of Kinds in the reign of another 1458. Death 1459 (RHKn.). He sold his farm Smedjeby on Öland in 1453-06-
2 CONC 07, which he received from his uncle, Mr Vernike. (RHKn.). Married to (Pt III pp. 133-142) Christina Gunnarsdotter, who survived the husband, daughter of Gunnar Gylta to Påtorp and Märta Bragde. Children: Arvid Knutsson. The Swedi
2 CONC sh National Council and the lawman. Died 1497. See Tab. 4. Märta Knutsdotter. Married in 1487 to the county governor in Ås county in Västergötland Broder But or Butz, to Bragnum in Länghems parish, Älvsborg county, who in the arms
2 CONC  carried a Sparre and still lived in 1498, in his 2nd marriage (married 1st with Margareta Mårtensdotter, daughter by Mårten Svan and Ragnhild Håkansdotter). (SK.) Ingrid Knutsdotter. Married to Håkan Karlsson Tun, to Attorp, who 
2 CONC led an upright crescent against two stars in the weapon. Lived in 1478. Brita Knutsdotter. Married to Knut Halvardsson, who carried in the weapon half a star over the wave [Pt III pp. 133-142.]. Karin Knutsdotter [Pt III p. 133 14
2 CONC 2].
2 CONT
