1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Agnes of Strathearn==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Also known as Annot of Strathearn'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Malise Strathearn, Earl of Orkney, Strathearn, and Caithness and Marjory de Ross 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Erengisle Suneson, Earl of Orkney.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Erengisle died childless, "at a great age", many years later. He was buried in Vadstena monastery church. His last wife, Countess Ingeborg had several children from her first marriage with lord Bengt Turesson of the family of Kr
2 CONC aakerum.  Erengisle's own nephews and nieces (and sisters) were already dead, without further issue, the last of them, Christina Ulvsdotter of Rickeby, having died in c 1389. His paternal family had only first cousins to continue 
2 CONC the line (the Trolle, the Pipa, the Hammersta and the Snakenborg of Flishult presumably were lineages descending from such cousins).
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters==
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK+7865&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7865&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7865]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1360 December 21 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Earl Erengisle Suneson (of the Orkney Islands)''' announces that he has given all his estates on Öland to the Dominican sisters in Kalmar for the benefit of himself and his two wives, Märta and '''Annot,''' with the consent of 
2 CONC his heirs and relatives: first everything he owns in Vi and Kvarnstad in Källa parish and a farm in Vannborga in Alböke parish (now in Köping parish), which estates give 20 marks of calfskin annually. Furthermore, the estate he ow
2 CONC ns in Karlevi in ​​Vickleby parish and a farm in Bröttorp, another in (Norra) Möckleby and a third in Strandtorp (all in Norra Möckleby parish), which give 20 marks of calfskin annually. He gives this on condition that the sisters
2 CONC  celebrate specified masses and vigilios as long as the monastery stands and worship is celebrated there. If the monastery is moved or in any special way is put out of order, all the goods shall be given under Växjö Cathedral on t
2 CONC he mentioned conditions. The issuer and the city of Kalmar, the uncle Mr. (Kettil) Glysing and the brother-in-law Nils Jonsson and the sister Mrs. Märta Sunedotter seal. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id
2 CONC =6000000010420533056&photo_id=6000000143514219833&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#MaliseStrathearndied1271A Project MedLands Scotland Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MALISE ([1275/80]-before 1329).'''  Andrew Wyntoun’s Cronykil records that "Jhon and Alysandyre" had five sisters, the second of which married "Off Stratherne the Erle Malys" by whom she had "a swne…Malys"[794].  He succeeded h
2 CONC is father in 1313 as Earl of Strathearn.  '''married firstly AGNES,'''daughter of --- (-after Aug 1320).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "dominus Willelmus de Sowlis et comitissa de Strathern" were conv
2 CONC icted of high treason at a parliament in Scone in Aug 1320 and sentenced to life imprisonment[795].  '''married secondly ([1323]) as her first husband, JOAN Menteith,''' daughter of JOHN Menteith of Rusky & his wife --- (-after 20
2 CONC  Mar 1367).  She married secondly John Campbell Earl of Atholl, thirdly Maurice Moray Earl of Strathearn, and fourthly (before 9 Nov 1347) as his second wife, William Sutherland Earl of Sutherland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Earl Malise & his first wife AGNES had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          '''MALISE''' (-killed in battle Neville’s Cross 17 Oct 1346).  He succeeded his father as Earl of Strathearn.  He succeeded his cousin Magnus as Earl of Caithness and Orkney in [1323/29].  He resigned the earldom of 
2 CONC Strathearn [24 Sep/16 Dec] 1332 into the hands of Edward Balliol, was tried for treason in 1344 for so doing, but found innocent[796].  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Johannes Ranulphi comes Moraviæ ac
2 CONC  etiam comes de Strathern constabularius Scotiæ…David filius et heres David de Lindsay…Willelmus Fraser…" were killed at Durham 17 Oct 1346[797].  [798] '''married firstly MARY,''' daughter of ---.  '''married secondly ([1325/28])
2 CONC  MATILDA [Marjory] of Ross,''' daughter of HUGH Earl of Ross & his first wife Matilda Bruce (-after 1350).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Earl Malise & his first wife MARY had four children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* (a)       '''MATILDA'''  married  --- de la Arde, son of ---. 
2 CONT >>>>* (b)       '''EUPHEME'''
2 CONT >>>>* (c)       '''AGNES (-before 1360).  married ERNGILS, son of ---.  He was granted the title Earl of Orkney by the king of Norway in right of his wife but forfeited it in 1375[799].'''
2 CONT >>>>* (d)       '''ISABEL''' married WILLIAM St Clair, son of ---.  Lord St Clair. 
2 CONT * ii)         '''MARY'''  "Malisius comes Strathern" granted "terram de Abbercarny…que fuit Roberti filii Magni dicti de Strathern" to "Johanni de Moravia de Dromsygart…[et] heredibus suis de Maria filia nostra" by undated charter
2 CONC [800].  [801] '''married ([1319/22]) as his second wife, JOHN Moray of Drumsagard,''' co. Lanark, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
