2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Medieval transcriptions:  A 9, fol. 66r, RA 0201
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcriptions:  Örnhielm: III, p. 813
2 CONT * Nygren, LBH 3, p. 221
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Brocman: II Misc. 19:61
2 CONT * DS No. 6034 (for identification of Hemming Fox)
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  B 16, fol. 131, RA 0202
2 CONT * The brothers Holmger and Magnus Torkelsson and their brothers-in-law Harald Ernilsson and Karl Tuveson also appear in letters 1359 30/7 (SDHK no. 7574 ); cf., however, ÄSF I, p. 57, where 'Tuveson' is assumed to be a misspelling
2 CONC . The identification of the knight Magnus, whose patronymic icon has been omitted in ms (see note in the text apparatus), is made more difficult by the fact that several contemporary knights bore the name Magnus. Possibly refers t
2 CONC o Magnus Knutsson who was then Östgötalagman (ÄSF I, p. 12). He appears as a sailor together with pastor Harald in another land transfer in Skänninge (letter 1358 29/7, SDHK no. 7413 ).
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Lars Eriksson Sparre's copybook, hs B 15, fol. 298r, RA 0202
2 CONT * Alla vägar bär till Rom: 75 generationer från von Wachenfeldt och Uggla till, By Bjarne Persson - https://books.google.com/books?id=IqoyDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA94&lpg=PA94&dq=Harald+Ernilsson+(Gren)+%26+Torkelsdotter&source=bl&ots=FDcOrtJ
2 CONC LCL&sig=ACfU3U1W3Y86cN7SulMNjid_50zEy2HYvA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi84d_5oOnqAhW2FzQIHXYAC58Q6AEwCHoECAoQAQ#v=onepage&q=Harald%20Ernilsson%20(Gren)%20%26%20Torkelsdotter&f=false
2 CONT * Documents concerning the history of Scandinavia. Chronological register ..., Volume 4, Royal Society for the publication of manuscripts concerning the history of Scandinavia - https://books.google.com/books?id=oTYOAAAAQAAJ&dq=ce
