1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Philippus Axelsen Thott''' (died November 4, 1464 in Gotland) was a Danish Council of State.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the''' son of Axel Pedersen Thott and his second wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1456 he was''' the king's courtier and then got Tranekær with Langeland in pledge. He is not unlikely to have been knighted at Christian I's coronation in Sweden in 1457. In 1462, when he is referred to as the council of cou
2 CONC ncils, on the occasion of a new loan he had granted to the king, the mortgage on Tranekær was increased and he was also promised to keep the loan unchanged for 6 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In August 1464 he was among the Danish commanders who, after Christian I had left Sweden himself, capitulated to Stockholm. On his way there, he met his brother Erik and several Danish great men Gulland, and when the sheriff here,
2 CONC  brother Oluf, died at the same time (16 September 1464), the great men in question deployed Phillipus together with Oluf's widow Anne as managers of the island. But already on November 4 of that year he died at Gulland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had (at the earliest 1455) married Ermegård, daughter of Eggert Frille. When Phillipus died, Eggert Frille became the guardian of his daughter's children and acted on their behalf as governor of Tranekær county, but soon after 
2 CONC (at the latest in May 1467) the king sat down with power in possession of the county. The exact time is unknown; but it must have been after the meeting in Nykøbing 1466 (where Karl Knutsson's daughter Magdalena gets married to Iv
2 CONC ar Axelsen Tott and his daughter Beata with Arvid Birgersson Trolle, and thus the Thott genus joins the Swedish side). The property of Phillipus, too, has evidently been seized; but this was nevertheless agreed at a meeting in Kal
2 CONC mar 1472 to be given back to the heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tranekær was long disputed; but in the end the crown paid the mortgage to Phillipus's heirs, of whom Ermegård had married Bent Torbernsen Bille a few years after the man's death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She also outlived her third husband, who died in 1494; even she died in the time between April 13, 1503 and June 23, 1504.
