2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sixten Sparre of Tofta==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparre of Tofta
2 CONT
2 CONT (Sparre af Tofta).png
2 CONT
2 CONT This lineage, which during its short heyday period from the end of the 1200 century to the beginning of the 1400 century, was one of the most prominent in the Swedish SuperSaver, brought in the gun a red Sparre in Goldfields as we
2 CONC ll as Sparre of Vik and Sparre of Hjulsta, with which, however, no Relationship should be proven. However, except the gun Småland lineage, political merging and sealing contact for connection with the family Sparre of Vik, and for
2 CONC  members of both these nights can at the same time sealing contact with the family Sparre of Hjulsta be placed. In mödernet, The ancestor Abjörn the son of Sixten (d. 1310), who should have taken the Sparre gun from his mother, ha
2 CONC s been befryndad with two lågfrälse Småland and Västgötska families with the spare in the gun, within which the name Abjörn also existed.
2 CONT
2 CONT TAB 1
2 CONT Sixten. Was married to Ingrid Abjörnsdotter of Våxtorp (Voxtorp) in likanämnd SN in Östbo HD in Småland, who lived even 1310. Her Seal: Sparre plus three lilies, two above and one below
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ingrid, Dead no later than 1301 and was childless, whereas her morning gift was inherited by the mother and siblings. He Was married to the Knight Red Keldorsson (Färla, oreste Keldorssons), who appeared in Urkunderna in 1286 — 
2 CONC 1305, and was a castle bailiff At the royal palace in 1289.
2 CONT * Abjörn Sixten's son, 1295, died 1310, knight, councilor, Seneschal. See tab. 2.
2 CONT * Kristina. Lived 1310. She was probably the mother of the knight Magnus Nilsson's wife Ingrid (Ivar nilssons).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source - Sparre of Tofta - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Tofta
