2 CONT >>1.         ADELA de Flandre ([1065]-Apr 1115).  The Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin specifies that "filia primogenita Robert Frisonis et Gertrudis" was the wife of "Canuti regis Dacie", but does not give her name[287].  The Annales B
2 CONC landinienses name "Athelæ amitæ [Balduini comes]" as the mother of "Karolus"[288].  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana specifies that "Robertus comes cognomento Frisio" had three daughters "quarum prima nupsit Kanuto regi
2 CONC  Danorum, quam postea habuit Rogerus dux Apulie"[289].  Malaterra names the wife of "dux Rogerius" as "neptem Francorum regis Philippi filiam Flandrensium marchionis Roberti…Adalalam"[290].  She was regent in Apulia 1111-1114 for 
2 CONC her son Guillaume Duke of Apulia.  The Lamberti Audomariensis Chronica records the death "V Kal Apr" of "Athela ducissa Apuliæ…filia Roberti Flandriæ comitis, uxor Rogerii ducis", although the year is not specified[291].  m firstl
