2 CONT Dirk V (født ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17. juni 1091). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pieter (født ca. 1053), kannik i Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha (født ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), gift med Filip I av Frankrike i 1072. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Floris (født ca. 1055), kannik i Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Machteld (født ca. 1057) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (født ca. 1061), gift med grev Baudouin I av Guines. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Med Robrecht I fikk hun ytterligere fem barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robrecht II (født ca. 1065 – 5. oktober, 1111). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (død i 1115), først gift med kong Knud IV av Danmark. Sammen fikk de sønnen Karl den gode, som senere ble greve av Flandern. Hun giftet seg senere med Roger Borsa, hertug av Puglia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude, som giftet seg med hertug Thierry II av Lorraine. Sammen fikk de sønnen Thierry av Alsace, den senere greven av Flandern. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip av Loo. Hans uekte sønn Vilhelm av Ypres hadde også et krav på grevskapet Flandern. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogiva, abbedisse
2 CONT
2 CONT . Gertrud av Sachsen, Gertrud Billung, född 1028/1035, död 1113/1115, begravd i Flandern, grevinna av Holland och Flandern. Dotter till hertig Bernhard II av Sachsen (död 1059) och Eilika av Schweinfurt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrud gifte sig första gången omkring 1050 med greve Florenz I av Holland (mördad 1061). I sitt 1063 ingångna andra äktenskap med greve Robert I av Flandern (död 1093) blev hon mor till Adele av Flandern.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Gertrud av Sachsen, född 1152/1155, död 1196/1197, begravd i Roskilde domkyrka i Danmark, hertiginna av Schwaben och drottning av Danmark. Dotter till hertig Henrik Lejonet av Sachsen och Bayern (död 1195) i dennes första gifte
2 CONC  med Klementia av Zähringen (död 1173/1178).
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrud gifte sig första gången 1 juni 1166 med hertig Friedrich IV av Schwaben (1144/1145-1167) och andra gången 1171/1177 med kung Knut VI Valdemarsson av Danmark (1162/1163-1202).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude of Saxony (also known as Gertrude Billung) (c. 1030 – August 4, 1113), was the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt. She married Floris I, Count of Holland (c. 1017 - June 28, 1061) c. 1050, an
2 CONC d upon his death, her son Dirk V became Count of Holland. Since he was still young, she became regent.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Dirk V came into power, William I, Bishop of Utrecht, took advantage of the situation, occupying territory that he had claimed in Holland. Gertrude and her son withdrew to the islands of Frisia (Zeeland), leaving William to o
2 CONC ccupy the disputed lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian), the second son of Baldwin V of Flanders. This act gave Dirk the Imperial Flanders as an appanage - including the islands of Frisia west of the Frisian Scheldt. She 
2 CONC and her husband then acted as co-regents for the young count.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a total of seven children with Floris I:
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liege. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17 June 1091). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha (ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Machteld (b. ca. 1057) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guînes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From her second marriage to Robert I she had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II of Flanders (c. 1065 – October 5, 1111). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (d.1115), who first married king Canute IV of Denmark, and was the mother of Charles the Good, later count of Flanders. She then married Roger Borsa, duke of Apulia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude, who married Thierry II, Duke of Lorraine, and was the mother of Thierry of Alsace, also later count of Flanders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Loo, whose illegitimate son William of Ypres was also a claimant to the county of Flanders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogiva, abbess of Messines. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Gertrude of Saxony (c. 1030 – August 4, 1113), also known as Gertrude Billung, was a countess consort of Holland, and a countess consort of Flanders by marriage. She was regent of Holland during the minority of her son. Countess o
2 CONC f Holland.  She was the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt. She married Floris I, Count of Holland (c. 1017 – June 28, 1061) c. 1050, and upon his death, her son Dirk V became Count of Holland. Since 
2 CONC he was still young, she became regent.  When Dirk V came into power, William I, Bishop of Utrecht, took advantage of the situation, occupying territory that he had claimed in Holland. Gertrude and her son withdrew to the islands o
2 CONC f Frisia (Zeeland), leaving William to occupy the disputed lands.  [Countess of Flanders:  In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian), the second son of Baldwin V of Flanders. This act gave Dirk the Imperial 
2 CONC Flanders as an appanage - including the islands of Frisia west of the Frisian Scheldt. She and her husband then acted as co-regents for the young count.  Family and children:  She had a total of seven children with Floris I:
2 CONT  1.Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liege.
2 CONT  2.Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17 June 1091).
2 CONT  3.Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége.
2 CONT  4.Bertha (ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072.
2 CONT  5.Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége.
2 CONT  6.Machteld (b. ca. 1057)
2 CONT  7.Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guînes.
