2 CONT '''TAB 11'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Magnusson (son of Magnus Gregersson, tab. 3). First mentioned in 1328. Was a magistrate (sub-magistrate?) in Västmanland in 1335. Knighted sometime between 1335 and 1337, probably at King Magnus' coronation on 21 July 1336. 
2 CONC Last mentioned on 4 September 1340. Owned Benhammar, now Benhamra, in Vada, Vallentuna, Uppland after his maternal uncle Jedvard Filipsson ( Rumby family )
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Daughter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingegärd Johansdotter.''' Mentioned as a widow at Benhammar 1365—1390. Donated land in Bro hd in Uppland with her daughter to St. Klara monastery. Was first married to King Magnus justiciarius and council knight Trotte Peters
2 CONC son ( Ekaätten ), who is earliest mentioned in 1333 and was still alive in 1362 but was probably dead in 1363. Mrs. Ingegärd was remarried in 1367 to knight Henrik Reventlow , who was still alive in 1382 but was dead in 1390.
