2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ragvald Nilsson (Fargalt) and Ingegärd Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Geneology=  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''gunman Nils Ragvaldsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1- '''Ragvald Nilsson''' was born around 1328. He was district chief in Oppunda district in Södermanland. Married to Ingegärd Karlsdotter, daughter of Karl Dansson (Stjärnjälke) and Ingeborg Magnusdotter (Bjälboätten's illegitimat
2 CONC e branch).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Karl Ragvaldsson''' (mentioned 1382–1401).
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Ragvaldsdotter,''' married to Magnus Elofsson (Tandlaätten)
2 CONT * '''Magnus Ragvaldsson the squire''' (mentioned 1399–1419). Married to ? 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Child''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ragvald Magnusson (Fargalt)''' (1426–1469) married to Katarina Svensdotter (Pik).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Child''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peder Ragvaldsson (Fargalt),''' mentioned for the last time in 1499, with him the family seems to have died out on the male side.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margareta Pedersdotter''' was married to the gunsmith Klas Kyle.
2 CONT * '''Karin Pedersdotter,''' married to her sister's brother-in-law the gunsmith and lawman on Öland Johan Kyle (brother of Klas Kyle).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fargalt Fargalt, by Wikipedia] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fargalt is a modern name for a Swedish noble family that had a wild boar, or fargalt, in its coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT The boar in the coat of arms is indicated in the painted coat of arms in Tövsala church as black and yellow, and is indicated by the antiquarian Johan Peringskiöld as a black boar in a field of gold.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family was from Södermanland and came to belong to the High Salvation. The oldest known member of the family is Ragvald Karlsson who in 1334-1335 seals letters with his seal. Judging by the seal, patronymic icon and hometown, 
2 CONC the gunsmith Nils Ragvaldsson is his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Ragvaldsson had property in Finspånga in Östergötland. He is mentioned in the sources 1342–1349. He is apparently the Nils Ragvaldsson, who
2 CONT together with his sons Ragvald and Anders were excommunicated in 1358 for abuse of a servant of the priest in Skällvik, Hammarkind's district in Östergötland. He also had a third son named Magnus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Not much is known about Anders Nilsson and Magnus Nilsson. Anders is mentioned in 1356 and possibly 1370. Magnus is mentioned in 1354 and 1360.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragvald Nilsson was born around 1328. He was district chief in Oppunda district in Södermanland in 1355 and again in 1356. He suffered a "stroke" on August 23, 1374 and became "warped in the face and paralyzed in half of the body"
2 CONC . Through a roll of the dice, it was decided that it should be called even then as the holy Birgitta Birgersdotter. Ragvald took a pilgrim's vow and the paralysis began to subside. He made a pilgrimage to Vadstena and became there
2 CONC  "completely healthy, rosy in the face and with a well-born body". No later than 1354, he married Ingegärd Karlsdotter. She was the daughter of Karl Dansson (Stjärnjälke) and Ingeborg Magnusdotter (Bjälboätten's illegitimate branc
2 CONC h).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragvald Nilsson had a daughter and two sons, the prebend in Strängnäs Karl Ragvaldsson (mentioned 1382–1401) and the squire Magnus Ragvaldsson (mentioned 1399–1419). The latter owned Hedensö and Gräfseboda (now Haneberg in Eskilst
2 CONC una) and land in Södermanland. His sister Ingeborg Ragvaldsdotter was married to Magnus Elofsson (Tandlaätten).[1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The lawman and Riksdag Erik Ragvaldsson (1463–1494), son of Ragvald Magnusson (Fargalt) (1426–1469) and Katarina Svensdotter (Pik) belonged to the same family. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT With the Riksdag and lawman in Södermanland's law saga, Peder Ragvaldsson (Fargalt), mentioned for the last time in 1499, the family seems to have died out on the male side. He left behind two daughters who married two brothers fr
2 CONC om the Kyle family, Margareta Pedersdotter was married to the squire Klas Kyle, and sister Karin Pedersdotter, was married to her sister's brother-in-law (brother of Klas Kyle), the squire and lawman on Öland Johan Kyle
2 CONT
