1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Bengt Larsson bjälke från Västergötland=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bengt Larsson belonged to a powerful, noble medieval dynasty known to modern historians as Lars Björnssons ätt (the clan of Lars Björnsson). The family bore a coat of arms featuring a single horizontal bar (en bjälke).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Marriage Confusions:''' There is a fictional Bengt Laurensson Rödbjälke", that have created online trees to split Bengt Larsson's real marriages across fake profiles. If you look closely at the Swedish family trees, you wil
2 CONC l find they have completely mixed up his wives: The Dowt Mix-up: Many online trees assign a wife named Margit Clausdotter Dowt to this family. Margit Dowt was actually married to a different Bengt entirely, but because of the fict
2 CONC ional "Rödbjälke" profile merges, she was accidentally dragged into a fictional family line.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Listed below are his correct wifes:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: ''' (1) Ingrid Karlsdotter (Stiernbielke) ''' Married in the 1350s (No children). Ingrid Karlsdotter passed away relatively young, likely in the late 1350s or 1360s, shortly after the family estate divisions. Because th
2 CONC ey had no surviving heirs, the properties that her father Karl Dansson had mortgaged to Bengt Larsson (SDHK-nr: 11853) reverted away from the Lars Björnsson family lineage. This property reversion explains why Ingrid's sister Inge
2 CONC gärd and her husband Ragvald Nilsson Fargalt spent decades fighting to reclaim those exact lands.
2 CONT * Married: ''' (2) Katarina Staffansdotter (Ulv)'''  Married around 1391 (Had daughter Ingeborg).  
2 CONT
2 CONT =Child with Katarina Staffansdotter (Ulv)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Bengtsdotter bjälke från Västergötland,''' Daughter of Bengt Larsson (bjälke) and his second wife Katarina Staffansdotter (Ulv). First Marriage: Bengt Tomasson (Pipa) (d. before 1442). He was a well-documented squire
2 CONC  who originally held the massive family properties of Bystad (in Asker, Närke). When Bengt Pipa died, Ingeborg was left as a relatively young, highly wealthy widow in control of his properties. She Second Marriage (ca. 1442): Lars
2 CONC  Siggesson "den äldre" (Sparre). When Lars Siggesson married her, he did so specifically as the "widow of Bengt Tomasson (Pipa).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003791053983&photo_id=6000000225647841999&position=0 Lars Björnsson bjälke Geneology Chart]
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225647841999&&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003791053983&photo_id=6000000225648232888&position=0 Summary Table of Verified Medieval Documents (SHK/ DS)]
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225648232888&&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk/?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=11853&Innehall=++&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermed
2 CONC eltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_11853&tab=post#tab SDHK number: 11853]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1381 February 26, : Place of issue: Outlaw Köping (Köping)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Content'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The marshal of the realm, knight Sten Bengtsson, the drost in Sweden Bo Jonsson, Folke Nilsson and Peter Djäken , under-secretary in Södermanland on behalf of Mr. Knut Karlsson, issue a writ of judgment. King Albrekt has in an ope
2 CONC n letter given the writsmen Folke Nilsson and Peter Djäken the authority to resolve a dispute between Ragvald Nilsson and Harald Kase regarding '''the property that Karl Dansson and his wife mortgaged to their son-in-law Bengt Lar
2 CONC sson. After examining the open letters of both sides and taking into account all the information they have obtained and heard, they cannot find anything other than that the property rightfully belongs to Ragvald Nilsson and those 
2 CONC who own the land with him.''' The writsmen therefore give the property to Ragvald Nilsson and reject Harald Kase's claim. The judgment is pronounced in the presence of the knights Erengisle Sunesson Earl, Bo Bosson, Birger Ulfsson
2 CONC , Staffan Ulfsson and Anund Jonsson and the squires Lars Björnsson and Ulf Jonsson. The issuers, knight Sten Bengtsson and drost Bo Jonsson, declare that Ragvald Nilsson and Harald Kase appeared before them at the same place, wher
2 CONC eupon Harald Kase was requested to completely renounce the property, and Ragvald Nilsson shall have no further claims on Harald Kase after this day. Thus they shall be in agreement and the dispute resolved. The issuers seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources''': Original:  Orig. on parchment (27.3 x 15.1 cm, fold 3.4 cm; 17 lines), Swedish National Archives (SE/RA/0101)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Post-medieval copies:  Misc. 74:3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT All the men who theta bref hear æll see how we Sten Beniczson ride e oc the march of the kingdom Bo Jonsson drozate j Swerike ‧ Folke Nicliss on ‧ oc Pæthar Dyekn vnd e rlaghman j Sudherma n na land e ‧ a ‧ h her ra Knwt Karlss on
2 CONC  s weghna æu e rdhelika m æth waro m Her ra ‧ Æpter thẏ høghborin første war kær e h er ra konu n g Albricht os Folka Nicliss on oc Pæthar e Dẏekn forsc ri phno m bøth oc befelde j sino opno breue ransaka oc vtleta ‧ sa n nẏnd oc 
2 CONC ræt vm the gothza delo who has been hafu e r mello m Raghuald Nicliss on oc Harald Kasa ‧ vm the gothz ther Karl Danss on oc hans wife hafdho pantsat thera magh Bæinct Lafrinzson oc os macht them mæth ræt atskilia ‧ gaf j samu bre
2 CONC fue tha hafuom wi thet ransakat oc vtleet ‧ æpt e r beggias thera opno brefuom oc m æth allom thøm bæzto m schælo m wi condom th e r til fa ælla høra ‧ oc æpter waro bæzto sa m witi so m wi viliom for e Gudhi ken nas tha wito m wi
2 CONC  eẏ rættar e æn thet sama gothz rætlika belongs to thøm forsc ri phna Raghwalde Nicliss on oc thøm th et agaar m æth ho no m . And for thẏ hafuo m wi Raghwalde Nicl is on th the same gothz tilvnnet oc toll from ‧ oc vndan Harald e
2 CONC  Kasa before erlikr a manna where her ra Eringisl e Sonas on s iærls sin ‧ her ra Bo Bosons ‧ her ra Birgher e Vlfsons ‧ her ra Staphan Vlfs on s ‧ and her ra Anu n dz Jonssons knights Lafrinz Biornss ons oc Vlf Jons on s swe na .
2 CONC  O ke n no m ps wi Sten Beniczson riddar a oc Bo Jonsson drotzte forsc ri phne at ther æpter a sama stath gingo the for nemp de Ragwal[ d ] Nicliss on oc Harald Kase for e eet mẏnne oc sæmio sculd til waar oc wi them for mynne sak
2 CONC t hafwm at Harald Kase scall ganzklika aflata thet sama gothz her til j delo standet hafu e r mello m hans oc Ragwald Nicliss on oc he m affonet war and Raghwalder Niclisson shall no indictment hafua until then for nemp da Harald 
2 CONC Kasa vm thet he opb[ out ]it hafu e r of thøm same research ri phna gothzom till that day. Oc ther mæth sculu the wara ‧ vinlika vm thessa gothza deelo excused. Oc til thessa thinga ‧ meere wisso oc witnisbẏrdh hafuom wi latet war
2 CONC  incighle her for e hænght. Date Laghløsakøpu n g, anno Domini Mccclxxxjº, feria tercia proxima post diem beati Mathie apostoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT * On the back: Eth dom breff, SEAL Seal: no. 1 only strip; no. 2 round of uncolored wax, diameter 3.0 cm (heraldic seal, see SMV I, p. 408): […]oecii Ionson; no. 3–4 only notches, DS no. 10340   see pdf of print Printed register R
2 CONC PB 1562
2 CONT * '''Literature and commentary:''' For the authors Sten Bengtsson (Bielke) and Folke Nilsson (Ivar Nilsson's family) see SRM with further references; for Peter (Torstensson) Djäken (Schack of Skylvalla), underling on behalf of Knu
2 CONC t Karlsson (Sparre of Tofta; see SRM p. 55), see J. E. Almquist in Släkt och hävd 1960, pp. 6 f. and p. 24, and the same in Lagsagor och domsagor i Sverige I (1954), p. 97, note 1. About the disputants, see for the squire Ragvald 
2 CONC Nilsson (Fargalt) ÄSF I, p. 30, and for Harald Kase ÄSF I, p. 299 f. About the witnesses Erengisle Sunesson (boat), titular earl of the Orkney Islands, Bo Bosson (Night and Day), Birger Ulfsson (Ulfåsaätten), Staffan Ulfsson (Wolf
2 CONC ), Anund Jonsson (Lion Face), Lars Björnsson (beam) and Ulf Jonsson (Aspenäsätten), see SRM with further references.
2 CONT The place of issue Köping is written in the letter Laglösaköping; on this name see H. Lindroth in Fornvännen 1918, pp. 213–223, and Swedish Place Name Dictionary (2016), p. 192 (under Köping). A large stain (which occupies about ⅓
2 CONC  of the letter) has made parts of the text only readable under UV light (see notes).
2 CONT
