1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Birger Gregersson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Gregers Johansson (Malstaätten) and Margareta Birgersdotter (Sparre av Hjulsta och Ängsö) 
2 CONT * Archbishop of Uppsala
2 CONT * born (probably) 1327, died (probably at Arnö castle by Mälaren) March 10, 1383, was a Swedish Catholic priest and bishop of the Uppsala diocese from 1366 until his death. In addition, he was the author of a legend about Saint Bi
2 CONC rgitta.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Catalog of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=100&Sokord=Johan+Johansson&EndastDigitaliserat=False&AvanceradSok=False&page=34&tab=post&FacettLimits=A9v_kw%3A0&postid=sdhk_'''10898 SDHK no: 10898''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 October 27''' 
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: Care eater''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000008258878255?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191614990826 '''Issuer: Archbishop Birger in Uppsala and Kettil Johansson''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger (Gregersson), archbishop of Uppsala,''' and Kettil Johansson transfer in the presence of Nils Petersson, subaltern in Uppland, and Gisle Uddsson 20 1/2 markland and 3 penningland of land, which estate they legally inheri
2 CONC ted from Birger's and his late brother Johan Gregersson's father and mother, their late aunt Katarina Johansdotter and uncle Tomas (Johansson), bishop in Växjö. Hereby, Birger receives 7 öresland of land in "Hesleby" in (Bond-)Arn
2 CONC ö parish, 1 öresland in Säby in the same parish, 17 öresland and 1 herbage land in Kunsta in Adelsö parish, 2 öresland in Malsta (in Malsta parish), 1 öresland in Lidö in Vätö parish, 21 öresland and 1 örtugland in Örby in Lagga p
2 CONC arish, 4 1/2 öresland in Ängeby in Börje parish and 1/2 arable land in Bergby in Vallentuna parish. Kettil Johansson receives 2 acres of land in Upplunda in (Roslags-)Bro parish, 2 acres of land in Malsta (in Malsta parish), 1 öre
2 CONC sland in Tälje in Frötuna parish, 4 öresland in Åkerö in the same parish, 1 öresland in Lidö (in Vätö parish), 17 öresland and 13 penninglands in Ekeby in Malsta parish, 12 öresland in Sund in (Roslags-)Bro parish, 1 /2 land in Ma
2 CONC rma in Lagga parish, 11 1/2 öresland and 6 penningland in Ängeby (in Börje parish), 1/2 land in Bergby (in Vallentuna parish) and 2 örtugland in Marjum in Söderby parish. Birger and Kettil Johansson each promise separately to neve
2 CONC r prevent the shift for the other party from now on. They further explain that two identical letters shall be drawn up on this parcel, one of which shall be kept by Birger, the other by Kettil. 1/2 land in Marma in Lagga parish, 1
2 CONC 1 1/2 öresland and 6 penningland in Ängeby (in Börje parish), 1/2 land in Bergby (in Vallentuna parish) and 2 örtugland in Marjum in Söderby parish. Birger and Kettil Johansson each promise separately to never prevent the shift fo
2 CONC r the other party from now on. They further explain that two identical letters shall be drawn up on this parcel, one of which shall be kept by Birger, the other by Kettil. 1/2 land in Marma in Lagga parish, 11 1/2 öresland and 6 p
2 CONC enningland in Ängeby (in Börje parish), 1/2 land in Bergby (in Vallentuna parish) and 2 örtugland in Marjum in Söderby parish. Birger and Kettil Johansson each promise separately to never prevent the shift for the other party from
2 CONC  now on. They further explain that two identical letters shall be drawn up on this parcel, one of which shall be kept by Birger, the other by Kettil.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The letter is sealed - like the other mentioned copy - by the knights Karl Ulfsson, lawman in Uppland, Arvid Gustavsson, lawman in Österland, further by (armsmen) Nils Petersson and Gisle Uddsson and by the issuers.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SEAL Seal: no. 1''' missing from the seal strip remaining in the letter; no. 2 round of brown wax, diameter 2.9 cm (heraldic seal, see SMV I, p. 208 and variant of Kettil Johansson's seal in letter 1382 11/7, RPB no. 1741): + S
2 CONC  Kettel (…) on (… ); no. 3 round of brown wax, damaged, diameter approx. 2.9 cm (heraldic seal, see SMV I, p. 118 and better preserved e.g. for letter 1374 8/9, DS no. 8639): + [S' K ]aroli ‧ W[lphs on militia]; No. 4 only minor f
2 CONC ragments of brown wax; no. 5 missing from the seal strip remaining in the letter; No. 6 only seal bag of purple linen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Additional text''' On the back: 62 Littera ‧ dominj ‧ B irgeri ‧ archiepiscopi Vpsal e n sis super divisione ‧ pre[ di ]orum f inter ipsum et Katillu m Joans on facta, Hesleby g vj (Uppsala cathedral's box sign; see L. Sjödin i
2 CONC n MRA 1939, p. 125) Drawing of Kettil Johansson's coat of arms (cf. SMV I, p. 208). Text on the seal strip to no. 6: (…) half ellopte markland oc t (…) g ortoghland jord ‧ (…) hær æpt er følghia ‧ j ‧ Wplund tw m a rkland jordh ‧ 
2 CONC j Telghiom ‧ j ‧ Frøtuna sokn eet […] .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=10811&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_10811&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab '''SDHK no: 10811''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 April 21''' 
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: (Bishop's) Arnö''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000008258771909?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191614703901 '''Archbishop Birger(Gregersson) in Uppsala'''] attributes (Confessor General Peter Olofsson in Vadstena Kloster) and thanks
2 CONC  for a sent legend about the Holy Virgin and asks the recipient of the letter to send the entire office about the Holy Virgin at the appropriate time. Furthermore, thanks for a recently sent letter, which mentions a revelation tha
2 CONC t the late wife Birgitta (Birgersdotter) had regarding this officium. Regarding the writing of the rhyming office ("composicionem hystorie") about Mrs. Birgitta, which the issuer has already sent to the recipient, except for the m
2 CONC ass office that is now being transmitted - with the exception of the sequence that was sent around Passion Sunday with Arvid Djäken - the archbishop does not want his own acumen to be attributed the merit of this, but praises the 
2 CONC Lord who has given his help thanks to the intercession of the Virgin Mary and wife Birgitta. Furthermore, the issuer points out that he found two errors in the rhyme scheme sent to the recipient of the letter. One error is found i
2 CONC n the prologue (that is, the first reading) and the other at the end of the ninth reading, where the day of (Birgitta's) translation to Vadstena monastery is mentioned. According to Mr. Karl, this did not take place on August 1 bu
2 CONC t in the month of July; the recipient of the letter is requested to correct this personally and to inform the issuer of the translation date, so that he can correct his own additions. In addition, the archbishop sends back a bundl
2 CONC e containing miracles, sealed with the seal of the issuer and provided with a notary mark. The recipient of the letter is asked to send the rhyme office together with the mass office to the bishop (Tomas Johansson) in Växjö, so th
2 CONC at he, who is the issuer's 'teacher and master', will correct what needs to be corrected. Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write
2 CONC  to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhortations. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith in the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and 
2 CONC Mr. Birger (Ulfsson). Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhorta
2 CONC tions. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith in the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson). Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulf
2 CONC sson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhortations. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith i
2 CONC n the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson).
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals with his secret.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Printed DS 9240  see pdf of print, C. Annerstedt (ed.), SRS III:2 (1871-1876), p. 206  C.-G. Undhagen (ed.), Birger Gregersson's Birgitta-officium (1960), pp. 24-25. Printed regest Reg. (no. 3) S. Engström in KÅ 1932, p. 273, se
2 CONC e also p. 274 ff.
2 CONT * Literature and commentary, See J. Liedgren, Archbishop Birger as a Latin prose stylist, KÅ 1980, p. 69
2 CONT
