1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ⚠️ '''WARNING: Fictional / Unhistorical Profile'''
2 CONT This profile is the result of faulty internet research and early 2000s amateur attempts to artificially bridge Danish royal history with Norwegian medieval nobility. '''In historical reality, a person named Anna Ranesdatter with t
2 CONC his biography never existed'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT 🧩 '''Why this profile is considered a fabrication''':
2 CONT * '''The Mixing of Two Nations and Lineages''': The listed father, Rane Jonsen Rani, was a real Danish knight executed in 1294 for his complicity in the murder of the Danish King Eric Klipping. He never had a daughter named Anna w
2 CONC ho moved to Norway.
2 CONT * '''An Artificial Link''': The profile of "Anna" was invented by internet genealogists merely to create a bridge between the Danish Rani family and the Norwegian Bolt family, attempting to explain the origin of the stars on the c
2 CONC oat of arms of the Norwegian Kane family.
2 CONT * '''Geographical and Chronological Absurdity''': Her birth at Gjørslev (Denmark) and death at Nesøya (Norway) are completely unsupported by any contemporary charters, deeds, or primary sources.
2 CONT * '''Conclusion''': Contemporary Norwegian and Danish medieval historians unanimously consider this connection and the person of Anna Ranesdatter to be an unproven fabrication.
