2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Isaksson , (son of Isak Björnsson, table 1), to Östanå in Riala parish, Stockholm county. Squire. Mentioned in letter 1405–1445-01-18. Was a member of the Riksråd, when he participated in the Kalmar meeting on 1438-07-09. M
2 CONC arried to Ingegerd Svensdotter, who lived on 1444-07-01, daughter of the squire Sven Pik, who bore a grey-white shell in a red field, and Cecilia, daughter of the Mecklenburg knight Gise van Helpten.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Isak Andersson.''' Lived in 1460.
2 CONT * '''Jakob Andersson .''' Squire. Jakob Andersson , (son of Anders Isaksson, table 2), to Östanå. Armsman 1450–1463. Married 1st to Kerstin Johansdotter . Married 2nd to Brita Månsdotter in her 1st marriage (married 2nd to Björn J
2 CONC önsson Pukehorn to Ulfsunda, who carried 2 wings in the coat of arms), daughter of the armorer and district chief Magnus Gustafsson (Tre rosar), to Frösvik, and Christina Laurensdotter (Blue).
2 CONT * '''Peder Andersson to Östanå,''' 1463.
2 CONT * '''Ericus Andreæ,''' enrolled at the University of Leipzig in 1442. Artium baccalaureus 1444-02-20 and mag. 1446-01-01 at the University of Leipzig. Provost in Uppsala 1463-01-26. Died 1504-05-07 and is buried in the main aisle 
2 CONC in Uppsala Cathedral [Bbl].
