2 CONT ==Project MedLands, Denmark Nobility, Chapter 2. Family of ULF Galicienfari==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ULF Jarl in Denmark "Galicienfari''' son of ? m '''BODIL Haakonsdotter,''' daughter of HAAKON Eriksson Jarl in Norway & his wife Gunhild of the Wends.'  Her marriage and parentage is given in Knytlnga Saga[27]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ulf & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.        ''' THRUGOT Ulfsen Fagrskinna,''' Commander of household troops of Svend I Estridsen King of Denmark.  m '''THORGUNNA''' daughter of VAGN Ågesen & his wife Ingeborg Thorkilsdatter 1070. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thrugot & his wife had three children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)        ''' THORKIL Thrugotsen (SVEND Thorgunnasen,)''' Florence of Worcester records that "Suani regis Danorum filii, Haroldus, Canutus et patruus eorum Esbernus comes et comes Turkillus" sailed from Denmark in [1069] and
2 CONC  landed "in ostio Humbræ fluminis"[28].  Commander of Knud II "den Hellige" King of Denmark.  1086.  m '''INGE,''' daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* b)         '''ASTRAD Thorgunasen''' Commander of Knud II "den Hellige/the Holy" King of Denmark.  1080.
2 CONT >>>>* c)         '''BODIL Thorgunnasdatter''' (-Mount of Olives near Jerusalem 1103).  She is named as the wife of Erik by Saxo Grammaticus, who also gives her father's and paternal grandfather's names[29].  The Liber Vitæ of Durh
2 CONC am names "Eiric rex Danorum Botild regina"[30].  m firstly BJØRN ---.  m secondly (before 1086) ERIK Svendsen, illegitimate son of SVEND II Estridsen & his wife ?  (Slangerup  Cyprus 10 Jul 1103, bur Cyprus).  He succeeded in 1095
2 CONC  as ERIK I "Ejegod/the Good" King of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands, Denmark Nobility - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DANISH%20NOBILITY.htm#UlfGalicienfariMBodilHaakonsd
