1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gleb Vseslavich''' (d. September 13, 1119, Kyiv) - Prince of Minsk since 1101, founder of the Minsk branch of the Polotsk princes dynasty, son of Prince Vseslav Bryachislavich.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1104, there was an attempt to besiege Gleb in Minsk, but unsuccessfully. Organizers of the siege were voivode Putyata, Oleg Svyatoslavich and Yaropolk Vladimirovich, the son of Vladimir Monomakh. In 1106, Gleb participated in a
2 CONC  campaign against the Baltic tribe of the Semigallians.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1116, Gleb started a war with Monomakh and burned Slutsk. In response to this, Monomakh with his sons, as well as with Davyd Svyatoslavich and the sons of Oleg Svyatoslavich, moved onto Minsk. Sons of Monomakh captured Orsha an
2 CONC d Drutsk and besieged Minsk. Gleb began negotiations, and Vladimir Monomakh, not wanting to shed Christian blood during Lent, agreed to peace and returned Minsk to Gleb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite the terms of the peace, in 1119 Gleb began a new war. Mstislav Vladimirovich, the son of Monomakh, captured Gleb and brought him to Kyiv, where he died the same year.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: from 1090 Anastasia (d. 1159), daughter of Yaropolk Izyaslavich, Prince of Vladimir-Volynsky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rostislav (d. c. 1165), Prince of Minsk 1146-1151, 1159-1165 (?), Prince of Polotsk 1151-1159
2 CONT * Volodar (died after 1167), Prince Gorodtsovsky 1146-1167 (?), Prince Minsk 1151-1159, 1165 (?) - 1167, Prince Polotsk 1167
2 CONT * Vsevolod (d. 1159/1162), Prince Izyaslavsky 1151-1159, Prince Strezhevsky 1159 - until 1162
2 CONT * Izyaslav (d. 1134)
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#GlebVseslavichdied1119 Medlands
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00141419&tree=LEO
