1 OCCU Princess of France, Countess of Flanders, Countess of Auxerre, Comtesse de Corbie, Comtesse de Corbie, Comtesse de Coutances, , Countess of Normandy, Prinsessa av Frankrike, Duchesse de Normandie, comtesse de Flandre
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Adela of France,''' known also as Adela the Holy or Adela of Messines; (1009 – 8 January 1079, Messines), was, by marriage, the '''duchess of Normandy''' (January – August 1027), and '''countess of Flanders''' (
2 CONC 1035–1067). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other forms of her name are Adela, Adélaïde, Adelheid, Aelis and Alix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Robert II (the Pious) and Constance d'Arles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Baudouin V 'le Pieux', Comte de Flandre
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Baldwin VI of Flanders, (1030 † 1070)
2 CONT *     Matilda of Flanders (1032 † 1083). In 1053 she married William Duke of Normandy, the future king of England
2 CONT *     Robert I of Flanders, (1033-1093)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on France Capetian Kings:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#_Toc154137001
2 CONT
2 CONT ADELA de France (-Messines 8 Jan 1079, bur Messines, Benedictine monastery).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "soror…regis Henrici Adela" as wife of "Balduino Insulano"[213].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Alam comitissam Flandrensem" as the daughter of King Robert[214].  S
2 CONC he is named as daughter of King Robert in a manuscript whose attribution to Orderic Vitalis is disputed, which also refers to her marriage[215].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Kerrebrouck mentions her betrothal to Duke Richard "très jeune" but does not cite the primary source on which this is based[216].  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Richardus Nortmannorum dux" agreed grants of property to "Adela" on the occasion of their marriage by charter dated Jan 1026, which does not specify her parentage[217].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father gave her the seigneurie of Corbie as her dowry.  Ctss de Contenance.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She founded the Benedictine monastery at Messines near Ypres.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Denis records the death "VI Id Jan" of "Adelaidis comitissa"[218].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (Jan 1027) to RICHARD III Duke of Normandy, son of RICHARD I Duke of Normandy & his first wife Judith de Bretagne ([1001]-6 Aug 1027).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Amiens 1028) BAUDOUIN de Flandre, son of BAUDOUIN IV "le Barbu/Pulchrae Barbae" Count of Flanders & his first wife Ogive de Luxembourg ([1012/13]-Lille 1 Sep 1067, bur Lille, Saint-Pierre).  He succeeded his father in 1035 as B
2 CONC AUDOUIN V “le Pieux/Insulanus” Count of Flanders.  He was regent of France for his nephew Philippe I King of France 1060-1066/67.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Flanders:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#BaudouinVdied1067B
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps05/ps05_230.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide (also known as Adelisa of France, and Adele-Alice or even Aelicie) may be daughter of Robert II and another wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [AR7],[Weis1],[ES],[PlantagenetA],[RFC],[Paget1]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Note:  She was the sister of Queen Matilda of England and widow of Richard 111, Duke of Normandy who dsp the uncle of William the Conqueror who married Baldwin V. de I'Isle, count of Flanders and of Artois.  Father also shown as H
2 CONC ugh Carpet King of France and mother as Adelheid. Adele is known as Countess d'Auxerre in band II of Europaische Stanntafeln (Marburg, Germany: Verlag Von J.A.Stargardt, 1984).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
