1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''BAUDOUIN VI Count of Flanders ([1030]-Hasnon Abbey 17 Jul 1070)'''
2 CONT s/o BAUDOUIN V "le Pieux/Insulanus" Count of Flanders. ([1012/13 ]-Lille 1 Sep 1067) & ADELA de France (1009-Messines 8 Jan 1079)
2 CONT x (1051) RICHILDE, wid/o HERMAN Comte de Hainaut (-Messines 15 Mar 1087, bur Hanson Abbey)
2 CONT *ARNOUL III Count of Flanders, Comte de Hainaut([1055]-killed in battle Cassel 22 Feb 1071, bur Saint-Bertin).
2 CONT *BAUDOUIN II Comte de Hainaut. ([1056]-on Crusade 1098, >8 Jun)
2 CONT *[AGNES (->1071)
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#BaudouinVdied1067A
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT BAUDOUIN, son of BAUDOUIN IV "le Barbu/Pulchrae Barbae" Count of Flanders & his first wife Ogive de Luxembourg ([1012/13]-Lille 1 Sep 1067, bur Lille St Pierre[222]).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names "Balduinum I
2 CONC nsulanum" as son of "Balduinum Barbatum [et] Odgivam"[223].  After 1028, he led a rebellion against his father who was forced to take refuge in Normandy.  After his father returned with reinforcements, Baudouin submitted but was a
2 CONC llowed to rule jointly[224].  He succeeded his father in 1035 as BAUDOUIN V "le Pieux/Insulanus" Count of Flanders.  He acquired overlordship of the county of Lens from the counts of Boulogne[225].  The Liber traditionum of Gant S
2 CONC aint-Pierre commemorates the donations of "Baldwinus junior marchysus filius Baldwini marchysi et Odgevæ comitissæ cum conjuge sua Adala", undated[226].  He took part in the Lotharingian rebellion against Emperor Heinrich III and 
2 CONC sacked the imperial palace at Nijmegen.  Emperor Heinrich gathered a large army to wreak revenge in 1049[227], but in practical terms the only loss to Flanders was the march of Antwerp[228].  Count Baudouin returned Valenciennes t
2 CONC o Hainaut, and thus indirectly to German suzerainty[229].  He maintained close relations with Godwin Earl of Wessex, first sheltering the latter´s son Svein after he was outlawed in 1049, then Earl Godwin himself when he was exile
2 CONC d from England in 1051.  Emperor Heinrich III invaded Flanders again in 1054 but had to retreat[230].  On the death of Henri I King of France in 1060, Count Baudouin became regent of France for his nephew King Philippe I.  The Ann
2 CONC ales Blandinienses record the death in 1067 of "Baldwinus potentissimus marchisus"[231]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Amiens 1028) ADELA de France, daughter of ROBERT II King of France & his third wife Constance d'Arles (1009-Messines 8 Jan 1079, bur Messines, Benedictine monastery).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names "filiam R
2 CONC odberti regis Francorum Adelam" wife of "Balduinum Insulanum"[232].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Alam comitissam Flandrensem" the daughter of King Robert[233].  Corbie was her dowry[234].  The Liber traditionum o
2 CONC f Gant Saint-Pierre commemorates the donations of "Baldwinus junior marchysus filius Baldwini marchysi et Odgevæ comitissæ cum conjuge sua Adala", undated[235].  She founded the Benedictine monastery at Messines near Ypres.  Phili
2 CONC ppe I King of France donated “villam in pago Parisiacensi sitam...Curtesiolum” to Saint-Denis, at the request of “amita mea soror...patris mei H...Adela”, by charter dated 1060, after 4 Aug[236].  The necrology of the abbey of Sai
2 CONC nt-Denis records the death "VI Id Jan" of "Adelaidis comitissa"[237]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Baudouin V & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.        ''' BAUDOUIN de Flandre ([1030]-Hasnon Abbey 17 Jul 1070).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names (in order) "Balduinum Haanoniensem, et Robdbertum cognomento postea Iherosolimitanum, et Matilde uxorem Guille
2 CONC lmi regis Anglorum" as the children of "Balduinum Insulanum [et] Adelam"[238].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names (in order) "Balduinum sextum, Robertum cognomento Fresonem, Philippum patrem Guilelmi de Ypra et fil
2 CONC ias duas Iudith, quam duxit Tostinus comes Nortdanimbronum in Anglia et Mathilda…Normannorum ducissa"[239], which confuses three generations of the family of the counts of Flanders.  Baudouin's father sent him to be educated at th
2 CONC e court of Emperor Heinrich III, who installed him as count in the march of Antwerp in [1045], although this was taken away in [1050] after his father opposed the emperor[240].  He succeeded in 1055 as BAUDOUIN I Comte de Hainaut,
2 CONC  by right of his wife.  He succeeded his father in 1067 as BAUDOUIN VI Count of Flanders.  The Annales Blandinienses record the death in 1070 of "Baldwinus marchisus, qui Hasnoni sepultus est"[241].  The Annales Elnonenses Maiores
2 CONC  record Baudouin's death "XVI Kal Aug" and his burial "Hasnonie"[242].  m (1051) as her second husband, RICHILDE, widow of HERMAN Comte de Hainaut, daughter of --- (-Messines 15 Mar 1087, bur Hanson Abbey).  The Annales Elnonenses
2 CONC  date the marriage of "Balduinus iunior Adele filius" to 1051 (although it incorrectly names his wife "Iudita"), specifying that thereby "castellum Monz obtinuit", and recording that the marriage was "consensu patris"[243] which p
2 CONC resumably refers to Baudouin's own father, maybe indicating that Baudouin was a minor at the time.  The difficult question of the parentage of Richilde is discussed fully in the document HAINAUT, which sets out her first husband's
2 CONC  family.  The Annales Blandinienses record that her husband's uncle Robert, having killed her son Arnoul Count of Flanders, captured his mother "Rikilde"[244].  Richilde married thirdly (1070) as his second wife, Guillaume FitzOsb
2 CONC ern Earl of Hereford.  The Annals of Winchester record the marriage in 1070 of “comitissam Flandriæ” and “rex…nepoti suo Willelmo filio Osberni”[245].  William of Malmesbury records that Baudouin I comte de Hainaut entrusted the g
2 CONC uardianship of his two sons to "Philip king of France…and to William Fitz-Osberne", adding that the latter "readily undertook the office that he might increase his dignity by a union with Richilda"[246].  The Complete Peerage, cit
2 CONC ing "Annales Flandriæ", states that Richilde was taken in battle where her new husband FitzOsbern was killed[247], but the precise reference has not yet been found to this primary source.  The necrology of Liège Saint-Lambert reco
2 CONC rds the death "XVII Kal Apr" of "Richildis comitisse"[248].'''  Count Baudouin VI & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ARNOUL de Flandre ([1055]-killed in battle Cassel 22 Feb 1071, bur Saint-Bertin).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names (in order) "Arnulfum et Balduinem" as sons of "Balduinum Haanoniensem [et] Richelde"[2
2 CONC 49].  "Arnulfum nepotem suum [Robertus filius Balduini comitis Insulani] occiso" is named in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin[250].  He succeeded his father in 1070 as ARNOUL III Count of Flanders, Comte de Hainaut.  "Arnulphus come
2 CONC s Flandrensium…cum matre mea Richilde et…fratre meo Balduino et sorore mea Agnete" donated "allodium…Thaviers in pago Hasbanie" to Ardenne Saint-Hubert, for the souls of "patris mei Balduini et comitis Herimanni", by charter dated
2 CONC  1071[251].  His uncle Robert rebelled against Count Arnoul, defeated him at the battle of Cassel where Arnoul was killed, and seized control of Flanders[252].  Arnoul's younger brother Baudouin was left only with the county of Ha
2 CONC inaut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         BAUDOUIN de Flandre ([1056]-on Crusade 1098, after 8 Jun).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names (in order) "Arnulfum et Balduinem" as sons of "Balduinum Haanoniensem [et] Richelde"[253].  Guibert describes
2 CONC  him as "Balduinus comes de Montibus, Roberti Flandrensis comitis iunioris patrui, filius"[254].  "Balduino frater eius [Arnulphum occiso]" is named in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin[255].  He succeeded his brother in 1071 as BAUD
2 CONC OUIN II Comte de Hainaut. -        COMTES DE HAINAUT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         [AGNES (-after 1071).  "Arnulphus comes Flandrensium…cum matre mea Richilde et…fratre meo Balduino et sorore mea Agnete" donated "allodium…Thaviers in pago Hasbanie" to Ardenne Saint-Hubert, for the souls of "patris mei
2 CONC  Balduini et comitis Herimanni", by charter dated 1071[256].  The mention of Comte Herman in this document suggests that Agnes was the same person as the unnamed daughter of "Hermannus filius ducis Thuringie ex Richilde" referred 
2 CONC to in the Annales Hanoniæ, which specify in a later passage that she became a nun[257].  If this is correct, she was Arnoul's uterine half-sister.] https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#BaudouinVdied1067A
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Baldwin VI of Flanders''' (c. 1030 – 17 July 1070) was briefly Count of Flanders, from 1067 to 1070. He was also (as Baldwin I) count of Hainaut from 1051 to 1070. He was the eldest son of Baldwin V of Flanders and Adele Capet,
2 CONC  a daughter of king Robert II of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Richilde de Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Arnoul III de Flandre
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Baudouin II de Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Agnes
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00018659&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baldwin_VI,_Count_of_Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT http://vls.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudewyn_VI_van_Vloandern
2 CONT
2 CONT http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudewijn_VI_van_Vlaanderen
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baudouin_VI_de_Flandre
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (Wikipedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin VI, Count of Hainaut, was one of the most prominent leaders of the Fourth Crusade, which resulted in the capture of Constantinople, the conquest of the greater part of the Byzantine Empire, and the foundation of the Latin 
2 CONC Empire, also known as Romania (not to be confused with the modern state Romania).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1051 he married Richilde, Countess of Mons and Hainaut, widow of count Herman of Mons. By this marriage Flanders took control of Hainaut (at that moment still a conglomerate of the county of Mons, the margraviate of Valencienne
2 CONC s and the southern part of the landgraviate of Brabant).
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin's early death left Flanders and Hainaut in the hands of his young son Arnulf III, with Richilde as regent. The countship was soon usurped by Baldwin's brother Robert the Frisian, who became count Robert I of Flanders. The 
2 CONC young Arnulf III was killed the next year at the Battle of Cassel (1071) and Baldwin's younger son eventually became Baldwin II of Hainaut.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Le cours de sa vie
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1045, il est investi momentanément par l'empereur Henri III de la marche d'Anvers. En 1051, son père lui fait épouser Richilde, veuve du comte Herman de Hainaut, et entre en possession de ce territoire où il devient Baudouin Ie
2 CONC r de Hainaut. Pour consanguinité, les époux sont d’abord excommuniés, puis une dispense papale est accordée. Les deux enfants de Herman sont privés de la succession de leur père : son fils Roger, deviendra en 1066 évêque de Châlon
2 CONC s-sur-Marne, sa fille entrera dans un monastère.
2 CONT
2 CONT En qualité de comte de Hainaut, il reconnaît entre 1066 et 1070 la guilde de Valenciennes (Karitet). Il restaure l'Abbaye de Hasnon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte de Flandre à la mort de son père (1067), son règne est marqué par la fondation de l’abbaye de Grammont (Geraardsbergen) qui reçoit des privilèges en 1068. Se sachant malade, il règle sa succession au cours de l’assemblée d’A
2 CONC udenarde : à l’aîné Arnould reviendra la Flandre, sous la tutelle de son frère Robert le Frison ; au cadet Baudouin le Hainaut, sous la tutelle de la comtesse Richilde, sa femme. En cas de décès de l’un de ses fils, l’autre hérite
2 CONC rait. Il est enterré au monastère d’Hasnon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Malgré ces précautions, la mort précoce de Baudouin laisse la Flandre et le Hainaut en contestation dynastique. Le comté de Flandre sera bientôt usurpé par Robert le Frison, qui deviendra Robert Ier de Flandre. Le jeune Arnoul III
2 CONC  sera tué l'année suivante à la Bataille de Cassel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage et enfants
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épouse vers 1051, Richilde, veuve du comte Herman de Hainaut. Celle-ci s'arrange pour déposséder les enfants de son premier mariage pour favoriser ceux de son second mariage. Sont issus de cette union :
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Arnoul III (1055 † 1071), comte de Flandre et de Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Baudouin II (1056 † 1098), comte de Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Agnès, vivante en 1071
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin VI of Flanders (c. 1030 – 17 July 1070) was briefly Count of Flanders, from 1067 to 1070. He was also (as Baldwin I) count of Hainaut from 1051 to 1070.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Boudewijn (Valenciennes, juli 1172 - spoorloos verdwenen in 1205) was als Boudewijn IX graaf van Vlaanderen van 1194 tot 1205, als Boudewijn VI graaf van Henegouwen van 1195 tot 1205, en als Boudewijn I keizer van het Latijns Keiz
2 CONC errijk van Constantinopel van 1204 tot 1205.
2 CONT
2 CONT [bewerk] Familie
2 CONT
2 CONT Hij was de oudste zoon van graaf Boudewijn V van Henegouwen en van Margaretha van de Elzas, zus en erfgename van Filips van de Elzas, graaf van Vlaanderen. Hij trouwde in 1186 met Maria, dochter van Hendrik I van Champagne. Bij de
2 CONC  dood van zijn moeder (15 november 1194) werd hij graaf van Vlaanderen en na het overlijden van zijn vader (17 december 1195) erfde hij ook het graafschap Henegouwen. Aldus waren beide graafschappen weer voor het eerst verenigd si
2 CONC nds Robrecht I de Fries zijn voorganger Arnulf III van Vlaanderen had verslagen.
2 CONT
2 CONT [bewerk] Bewind
2 CONT
2 CONT De eerste jaren van zijn bewind verliepen in een aanhoudende strijd met zijn leenheer, de Franse koning Filips II August, die enkele jaren voordien (1191) de hand had gelegd op het zuidelijke deel van Vlaanderen (Artesië). Boudewi
2 CONC jn zocht vooral steun bij de Rooms-Duitse Hendrik VI en de Engelse koning Richard I Leeuwenhart. Bij de Vrede van Péronne (1199) werd Filips II August verplicht een deel van Zuid-Vlaanderen te restitueren. Nog in hetzelfde jaar le
2 CONC gden Boudewijn en zijn echtgenote in de St.-Donatuskerk te Brugge de kruisvaartgelofte af: zodoende verliet hij op 14 april 1202 zijn graafschap om zich aan te sluiten bij de Vierde Kruistocht (1202-1204), die onder impuls van Ven
2 CONC etië niet het Heilige Land, maar Constantinopel als doel had. Tijdens zijn afwezigheid nam zijn echtgenote Maria van Champagne het regentschap in Vlaanderen en Henegouwen waar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nadat de kruisvaarders Constantinopel ingenomen en de legitieme keizer Alexios V verdreven hadden, werd Boudewijn op 9 mei 1204 tot eerste Latijnse keizer van Constantinopel uitgeroepen en op 16 mei in de Hagia Sophia gekroond. Me
2 CONC t paus Innocentius III spande hij samen om een eind te maken aan het Groot Schisma. Veel kon Boudewijn als keizer niet realiseren, want reeds in april van het volgende jaar viel hij in handen van de Bulgaarse tsaar Kalojan. Sindsd
2 CONC ien werd nooit meer een spoor van hem teruggevonden, zodat de graafschappen Vlaanderen en Henegouwen in handen kwamen van zijn minderjarige dochter Johanna. Zijn vrouw, die hem was achterna gereisd, overleed onderweg te Akko (voor
2 CONC jaar 1204). In Constantinopel werd hij opgevolgd door zijn broer Hendrik.
2 CONT
2 CONT Volgens de lokale folkore in Veliko Tarnovo, hoofdstad van het Tweede Bulgaarse Koninkrijk, werd Boudewijn gevangen gezet in een toren in de muur van de vesting Tsarevets. Dit torentje is nog altijd (in herstelde staat) te zien en
2 CONC  wordt lokaal Boudewijns Toren genoemde. Alberik van Troisfontaines verhaalt voorts dat Boudewijn de avances van een Bulgaarse koningin afsloeg, die hem prompt van poging tot verkrachting beschuldigde en hem liet executeren. De Bu
2 CONC lgaarse vorst Joannitsa zou opdracht hebben gegeven Boudewijns lichaam in stukken te hakken en aan de honden te voederen. De honden zouden echter geweigerd hebben zijn lichaam te eten. Twintig jaar later verscheen er in Vlaanderen
2 CONC  een kluizenaar ten tonele die beweerde de verloren gewaande Boudewijn te zijn. Niettegenstaande hij erin slaagde enige volgelingen om zich heen te verzamelen, werd de man als bedrieger terechtgesteld.
2 CONT
2 CONT [bewerk] Trivia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2005 werd hij genomineerd voor de titel van De Grootste Belg. Hij eindigde echter buiten de nominatielijst op nr. 197.
2 CONT
