1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Matilde Maud de Flandre (van Vlaanderen),''' Matilda of Flanders, styled Queen Consort Matilda of England on 11 May 1068.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Flanders (c. 1031 – 2 November 1083) was Queen consort of the Kingdom of England and the wife of Guillaume (William) I the Conqueror, King of England and Duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Count Baldwin V of Flanders, and Adèle (1000-1078/9), daughter of Robert II of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents:''' Baudouin V 'le Pieux', Comte de Flandre & Alix Capet<br/>
2 CONT '''Spouse:''' Guillaume (William) I the Conqueror, king of England and Duke of Normandy
2 CONT ====Children:====
2 CONT # Robert Curthose (c. 1054 – 1134), married Sybil of Conversano
2 CONT # Adeliza (or Alice) (c. 1055 – ?), uncertain
2 CONT # Cecilia (or Cecily) (c. 1056 – 1126)
2 CONT # William Rufus (1056 – 1100)
2 CONT # Richard, Duke of Bernay (1057 – c. 1081)
2 CONT # Alison (or Ali) (1056 -c. 1090)
2 CONT # Adela (c. 1062 – 1138), married Etienne de Blois
2 CONT # Agatha(c. 1064 – c. 1080)
2 CONT # Constance (c. 1066 – 1090), married Alan IV Fergent
2 CONT # Matilda (very obscure, her existence is in some doubt)
2 CONT # Henry Beauclerc (1068–1135)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==NOTE==
2 CONT There is NO evidence she married a Gerbod as well - see comments
2 CONT
2 CONT ==LINKS==
