2 CONC , with Tewkesbury, various lordships inWorcester, Gloucester, Somerset, and other counties. Maud [Matilda],afterwards wife of WILLIAM THE CONQUERER, in her youth wished tomarry Brictric, who refused her. When she became Queen, she
2 CONC imprisoned him, and on his death shortly afterwards his manors, the
2 CONT (later) honour of Gloucester, were given to her.
2 CONT For many years it was assumed that Gundred, who married William de Warrene, was a daughter of William I and Matilda (as indicated in The Plantagenet Ancestry).  However it is now known that Gundred was a daughter of Gherbod the Fl
2 CONC eming (as indicated in Ancestral Roots).  The following information strongly suggests that Gundred's mother was Matilda (thus the mistaken notion that she was daughter of William I).
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------- -----------------
2 CONT copied from Bill Crawford's ancestry: crawfolk data base on World Connect Project, rootsweb.com
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------- -----------------
2 CONT
