1 NOTE At 4'2" (127 cm) tall, Matilda was Britain's smallest adult queen, according to the Guinness Book of Records.
2 CONT ***
2 CONT There were rumours that Matilda had been in love with the English ambassador to Flanders, a Saxon named Brihtric, who declined her advances. Whatever the truth of the matter, years later when she was acting as Regent for William i
2 CONC n England, she used her authority to confiscate Brihtric's lands and throw him into prison, where he died.
1 NOTE <table width=610><tr align=left valign=top>
2 CONT <td valign=top><table border="1" align="center" width="220"><tr><td bgcolor=ffffff><img src="http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/images/royalty/matilda-flanders.jpg"alt="Image of Queen Matilda of Flanders" width="200" align="center"
2 CONC ></img><br clear="all"></br><center>Queen Matilda of Flanders<br>1031-1083<br><i>from "Queens of England" - 1894 - provided by Cindy Jackola.</i></br><!-- 2871 --></td></tr></table></td>
2 CONT </tr><tr align=left valign=top>
