1 OCCU Queen of the Franks (1072-1092), Reine consort des Francs
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bertha of Holland (c. 1055–1094) was the first wife and queen of Philip I of France, King of France.The marriage was nullified by virtue of her husband's bigamy. She did not survive long after.  Bertha was confined
2 CONC  to the fortress of Montreuil-sur-Mer, part of her dower land.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > ''~• died at [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Citadelle_de_Montreuil-sur-Mer.jpg the Chateau de Montreuil-sur-Mer] .'' Français : Vue aérienne de la citadelle de Montreuil-sur-Mer (Pas-de-Calais) XIIIe -XIXe siècle
2 CONT Date of photo:	18 March 2014,
2 CONT > ''the construction of the citadel seems to have post-dated Bertha's death by a few decades.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Coordinates: 50°27′53″N 1°45′47″E
2 CONT From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montreuil-sur-Mer Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of (Florent I) Floris I, Count of Holland, by his wife Gertrude of Saxony, the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony. After her father died in 1061, her mother remarried to Robert I, Count of Flanders, called
2 CONC  Le Frisian. In 1072 her stepfather concluded a peace treaty with King Philip. As part of the terms of the treaty Bertha was married to Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nine years passed before Bertha produced the desired son and heir, Louis. Reportedly, her fertility was only restored thanks to the prayers of a hermit, Arnoul, who also named the child. Together, Philip and Bertha had five childr
2 CONC en:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Constance, married Hugh I of Champagne before 1097 and then, after her divorce, to Bohemund I of Antioch in 1106  
2 CONT # Louis (December 1, 1081–August 1, 1137)  
2 CONT # Henry (b. 1083) (died young)  
2 CONT # Charles (b. 1085) abbot of Charlieu Abbey  
2 CONT # Eudes (1087-1096)  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1092, Philip repudiated Bertha, alleging that she was too fat. He confined her to the fortress of Montreuil-sur-Mer, and took up with Bertrade de Montfort, the countess of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Philippe Ier de FRANCE and Berthe de HOLLANDE
2 CONT
2 CONT [10403] FRANCE (de), Philippe Ier (Henri Ier & Anne de KIEV ou de RUSSIE [10404]), roi de France, born 1053, died 1108-07-29 Melun (Seine-et-Marne : 770288), France, buried Saint-Benoît-sur-Loire (Loiret : 450270), France
2 CONT
2 CONT * married 1071 or 1073 .. (France)
2 CONT
2 CONT HOLLANDE (de), Berthe (..)
2 CONT
2 CONT       1) Louis VI le Gros, roi de France, born about 1078, died 1137-08-01 Paris (Paris : 750056), France, buried Saint-Denis (Seine-Saint-Denis : 930066), France, married .. (France) 1115 Adélaïde de SAVOIE
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Histoire de la maison royale de France (Père Anselme); Mémoires (Société généalogique canadienne-française) 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/010/010403.php
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Filha do conde Florent I da Holanda e de Gertrude de Saxe, era neta materna de Bernardo II, duque da Saxónia. Depois da morte do seu pai em 1061, a sua mãe voltou a casar-se com Roberto I, conde da Flandres. Em 1072, este acordou 
2 CONC uma aliança política com Filipe I de França, que incluía o seu casamento com o monarca francês.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berta só gerou um herdeiro nove anos depois. A lenda popular conta que a sua fertilidade só foi restaurada graças às orações de um eremita, Arnaldo, que deu o nome de Luís à criança.
2 CONT
2 CONT Em 1092 Filipe enamorou-se de com Bertranda de Monforte, condessa de Anjou, e repudiou Berta alegando consanguinidade, uma vez que eram primos afastados. Aprisionada pelo rei francês na fortaleza de Montreuil-sur-Mer, lá morreria 
2 CONC a 30 de Julho de 1094.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Holland (c. 1055–1094) was the first wife and queen of Philip I of France, King of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of (Florent I) Floris I, Count of Holland, by his wife Gertrude of Saxony, the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony. After her father died in 1061, her mother remarried to Robert I, Count of Flanders, called
2 CONC  Le Frisian. In 1072 her stepfather concluded a peace treaty with King Philip. As part of the terms of the treaty Bertha was married to Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nine years passed before Bertha produced the desired son and heir, Louis. Reportedly, her fertility was only restored thanks to the prayers of a hermit, Arnoul, who also named the child. Together, Philip and Bertha had five childr
2 CONC en:
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance, married Hugh I of Champagne before 1097 and then, after her divorce, to Bohemund I of Antioch in 1106 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (December 1, 1081–August 1, 1137) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry (b. 1083) (died young) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles (b. 1085) abbot of Charlieu Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes (1087-1096) 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1092, Philip repudiated Bertha, alleging that she was too fat. He confined her to the fortress of Montreuil-sur-Mer, and took up with Bertrade de Montfort, the countess of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Holland (c. 1055–1093) was the first wife and queen of Philip I of France, King of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Floris I, Count of Holland, by his wife Gertrude of Saxony, the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony. After her father died in 1061, her mother remarried to Robert I, Count of Flanders, called Le Frisian.
2 CONC  In 1072 her stepfather concluded a peace treaty with King Philip. As part of the terms of the treaty Bertha was married to Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nine years passed before Bertha produced the desired son and heir, Louis. Reportedly, her fertility was only restored thanks to the prayers of a hermit, Arnoul, who also named the child. In 1092, Philip repudiated Bertha, alleging
2 CONC  that she was too fat. He confined her to the fortress of Montreuil-sur-Mer, and took up with Bertrade de Montfort, the countess of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Together, Philip and Bertha had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Constance, married Hugh I of Champagne before 1097 and then, after her divorce, to Bohemund I of Antioch in 1106
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Louis (1 December 1081–1 August 1137)
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Henry (b. 1083) (died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Charles (b. 1085) abbot of Charlieu Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Eudes (1087-1096)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
