1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_of_Ypres
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Ypres (c. 1090 – 24 January 1164/1165), styled count of Flanders, was King Stephen of England's chief lieutenant during the English civil wars of 1139–54 (known as the Anarchy). He commanded a contingent of Flemish sold
2 CONC iers. He claimed the county of Flanders upon the death of Charles the Good on 2 March 1127/28.
2 CONT
2 CONT Though no proof exists of his creation as Earl of Kent by King Stephen, chroniclers describe him as "possessing the county" and "having Kent in his custody". He exercised the same powers over this county as other earls over theirs
2 CONC ; though he never adopted the comital (of a count or earl) style.
2 CONT
2 CONT He founded the Cistercian house of Boxley circa 1146.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an illegitimate son of Philip of Loo, son of Robert I, Count of Flanders and Gertrude of Saxony. He was a claimant in 1119 to the title of Count of Flanders but lost the claim to Charles the Good; and again in 1127, when he
2 CONC  lost to William Clito. The chronicle of Galbert of Bruges attributes his failure to his illegitimate birth. He sought the title again the following year (1128) after William Clito's death, but lost to Thierry of Alsace, who banis
2 CONC hed him from Flanders in 1133.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Guillaume Ypres (ca 1090 - 24 januari död. 1162, 1164 eller 1165,), Borgmästare av Ypres och sedan guvernör i Kent, var en olycklig pretendent (person som gör anspråk på makt, oftast kunglig sådan) p.g.a. länet av Flandern år 1119
2 CONC  och sedan 1127- 1128. Han spelade en viktig roll som kapten för legosoldater till Stephen, kung av England, under inbördeskriget för kronan .
