2 CONT Adelaide of Leuven (died c. 1158) was the wife of Simon I, Duke of Lorraine (1076-1138). She was the daughter of Henry III of Leuven and his wife Gertrude of Flanders. After the death of her husband, Adelaide retired to a Cisterci
2 CONC an abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Simon I and Adelaide included:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Matthias I, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT     * Robert, Lord of Floranges
2 CONT     * Agatha of Lorraine, wife of Renaud III, Count of Burgundy
2 CONT     * Hedwige, wife of Frederick III, count of Toul
2 CONT     * Bertha, wife of Margrave Hermann III of Baden
2 CONT     * Mathilde, wife of Gottfried I, Count of Sponheim
2 CONT     * Baldwin
2 CONT     * John
