2 CONC he father's side and of the Swedish king Olaf Eirikson by the mother's side, for her mother was Queen Sigrid the Haughty, a daughter of Skoglar Toste".  Morkinskinna names “the lady Ástrídr…sister of two kings, Knútr the Great and
2 CONC  Óláfr the Swede” as daughter of “King Sveinn Forkbeard…and Sigrídr en stórráda” who had previously been married to King Eirikr enn sigrsæli” and wife of “Jarl Úlfr sprakalegge”.  Adam of Bremen records that "Chnud…rex Danorum" ga
2 CONC ve "suam…germanam Margaretam pro foedere" to "comitis Nortmannorum Rikardi" and, after she was repudiated by Richard, to "Wolf duci Angliæ".  Saxo Grammaticus also records her betrothal.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (after 1017) to RICHARD II "le Bon/l'Irascible" Duke of Normandy, son of RICHARD I "Sans Peur" Comte [de Normandie] & his second wife Gunnora --- (-23 Aug 1026).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (after 1017) to ESTRID [Margrete] Svendsdatter, daughter of SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark & his second wife Sigrid “Storråda/the Haughty” (-9 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>, bur Roskilde Cathedral). Adam of Brem
2 CONC en records that "Chnud…rex Danorum" gave "suam…germanam Margaretam pro foedere" to "comitis Nortmannorum Rikardi" and after, she was repudiated by Richard, to "Wolf duci Angliæ". Saxo Grammaticus also records her betrothal. She la
2 CONC ter married Ulf Thrugilson Jarl [Wulfsige Sprakeling]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ULF Thrugilson Jarl [Wulfsige Sprakeling], son of SPRAKLING [Thrugils Sprakaleg] in England & his wife --- (-murdered Roskilde 1026).  Jarl in England 1017.  Regent of Denmark from 1026.  He joined the alliance of Olav II King o
2 CONC f Norway and Anund King of Sweden to oppose his brother-in-law King Knud.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ULF Thrugilson [WULFSIGE Sprakeling] (-murdered Roskilde 1026).  Florence of Worcester specifies that he was the son of "Spracing".  Snorre names Earl Ulf as son of Thorgils Sprakaleg.  Jarl in England 1017.  Regent of Denmark fro
2 CONC m 1026.  He joined the alliance of Olav II King of Norway and Anund King of Sweden to oppose his brother-in-law King Knud.  He was killed on the orders of King Knud whom he had allegedly insulted.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ESTRID [Margrete] Svendsdatter, daughter of SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark & his wife his second wife Sigrid “Storråda/the Haughty” (-9 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  Adam of Bremen records tha
2 CONC t "Chnud…rex Danorum" gave "suam…germanam Margaretam pro foedere" to "comitis Nortmannorum  Rikardi" and after she was repudiated to "Wolf duci Angliæ".  Snorre names "Astrid, a daughter of King Svein Forkbeard" as wife of Earl Ul
2 CONC f.  Morkinskinna names “the lady Ástrídr…sister of two kings, Knútr the Great and Óláfr the Swede” as daughter of “King Sveinn Forkbeard…and Sigrídr en stórráda” who had previously been married to King Eirikr enn sigrsæli” and wif
2 CONC e of “Jarl Úlfr sprakalegge”.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf & his wife had [four] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             SVEND Estridsen ([1020]-Søderup [29] Apr 1074, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  Adam of Bremen names "Bern ducem et Suein regem" as sons of "Wolf duci Angliæ" & his wife[276].  Jarl 1042.  He succeeded in 1047 as SVEND II 
2 CONC King of Denmark. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below, Part B. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             BJØRN Ulfsen (-murdered Dartmouth 1049, bur Dartmouth, transferred to Winchester Cathedral).  Adam of Bremen names "Bern ducem et Suein regem" as sons of "Wolf duci Angliæ" & his wife.  1020.   Florence of Worcester
2 CONC  specifies that he was the son of Ulf and brother of King Svend.  He was created Earl in Eastern Mercia in 1045 by Edward "the Confessor" King of England.  King Edward granted him part of the earldom of Svein Godwinsson, son of Go
2 CONC dwin Earl of Wessex, after the latter was outlawed following his seduction of the Abbess of Leominster.  Bjørn was killed on board the ship of his cousin Earl Svein, son of Godwin Earl of Wessex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             ASBJØRN Ulfsen (-1086).  Adam of Bremen names "in Anglia duces…Bern…[et] Osbern" as brothers of "Suein regis".  As Asbjørn is not named with his brothers in the earlier passage which names their mother, it is possib
2 CONC le that he was their half-brother born from a concubine.  Like his brother, he lived in England.  Jarl in Denmark.  Florence of Worcester records that "Suani regis Danorum filii, Haroldus, Canutus et patruus eorum Esbernus comes e
2 CONC t comes Turkillus" sailed from Denmark in 1069 and landed "in ostio Humbræ fluminis".  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Asbjørn's wife is not known.  Asbjørn & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               MARGRETE Asbjørnsdatter .  Her marriage is referred to in Knytlinga Saga[282].  A Queen Margreta is referred to in the Liber daticus Roskildensis who was assigned to King Harald III in the 19th century[283].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m her first cousin, HARALD III "Hein/the Whetstone" King of Denmark, illegitimate son of SVEND II Estridsen King of Denmark (-17 Apr 1080, bur Dalby Cloister, near Lund). 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)             [daughter .  m ---.]  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               ASMUND "Free-booter" (-killed in battle [1063]).  Snorre names "Asmund…said to have been King Svein's sister's son and his foster-son" when recording that he was murdered[284].  Morkinskinna records that “Ásmundr”
2 CONC  was the son of “Bjorn” (see above)[285].  
