2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Estrid var en af de store kvindeskikkelser i overgangsperioden mellem den hedenske vikingetid og den kristne middelalder. Hendes moder skal således have nægtet at lade sig omvende til kristendommen, mens Estrid selv som enke sørge
2 CONC de for, at den første stenkirke blev bygget i Danmark. Det var en kaotisk periode, hvor kongerne havde nok at gøre med at holde sig på tronen. Pludselig kunne de mest oplagte tronfølgere være døde, og det kunne give fornemme kvind
2 CONC er som Estrid chancen for at tage magten. Især hvis de havde en lovende søn. Hun fik da også titel af dronning uden nogensinde at have været gift med en konge. Det bedste udtryk for hendes royale betydning i samtiden er det faktum
2 CONC , at hendes søn Sven som konge tog navn efter hende og kaldte sig Estridsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo van de Pas: Europäische Stammtafeln, J.A. Stargardt Verlag, Marburg, Schwennicke, Detlev (Ed.), Reference: II 97. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo van de Pas:  Nachkommen Gorms des Alten, 1978 , Brenner, S. Otto, Reference: 29.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ASTRYDA MAŁGORZATA - córka króla Swena Widłobrodego , siostra dwóch kolejnych królów duńskich Haralda Svenssona ( król Danii 1014 -1018 ) i Kanuta Wielkiego ( król Anglii 1016 - 1035 , Danii 1018 - 1035 , Norwegii 1028 -12 listopa
2 CONC da 1035 ) oraz matka króla Swena II Estrydsena .
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Astrid Sveynsdottir was born circa 997. She was the daughter of Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson, King of Denmark and England and Sigrid 'the Haughty' (?). She married Richard II, 4th Duc de Normandie, son of Richard I, 3rd Duc de N
2 CONC ormandie and Gunnor de Crêpon, between 1017 and 1027. She married Ulf Thorgilson, Earl in England, son of Thorgils 'Sprakalegg' Styrbjornson and Sigrid of Halland, circa 1018. She and Richard II, 4th Duc de Normandie were divorced
2 CONC  before 1024. Astrid Sveynsdottir was also known as Estrith.1 She was also known as Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships between historical figures could have been simplified or even fabricated in the text to give the impression that succession remained within the same family….Precise chronology is also difficult to assess from the Sag
2 CONC as….The conclusion must be that the tight family network described in the Sagas is unlikely to be correct and that the relationships shown below should be treated with considerable caution. http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIA
2 CONC N%20NOBILITY.htm
