3 CONT "Etymology (of the word Dronning)
3 CONT From Old Norse dróttning (“mistress, queen”), cognate with Swedish drottning. Derived from dróttinn (“lord, leader”) (Danish drot).
3 CONT
3 CONT Noun
3 CONT dronning c (singular definite dronningen, plural indefinite dronninger)
3 CONT
3 CONT queen (a female monarch)
3 CONT queen (the wife or widow of a king)
3 CONT (figuratively) queen (a person who is leading in a certain area)
3 CONT (zoology) queen (the reproductive female in social insect species)
3 CONT (chess) queen
3 CONT
