1 NAME Esger (Eskil) Torbjörnsson /Sparre över Sjöblad/
2 GIVN Esger (Eskil) Torbjörnsson
2 SURN Sparre över Sjöblad
2 _MARNM Sjöblad
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1380
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 12 APR 1439
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Esger (Eskil) Torbjörnsson Sjöblad=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Torbjörn Eskilsson Sparre över blad
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  1418 in Forstena,  the knight '''Esger (Eskil) Torbjörnsson (Sjöblad)''', Son of Torbjörn Torbern Eskilsson (Sparre över blad). This farm was formerly owned by a family that initially carried a lake leaf in the weapon,
2 CONC  which was subsequently changed to a rear head. Of this older Forstena family, the following are known. The brothers Åke and Esger Torbjörnssons appear during the years 1415–1435, the latter married 1418 at Forstena to '''Ingrid S
2 CONC iggesdotter, daughter of the gunman Sigge Birgersson, who is named in the documents 1405–1417 and in the arms carried a rear head, and apparently owned Forstena (he was 1413 resides in Väne hierad).''' Both of these brothers carri
2 CONC ed an unsheathed sea leaf or heart in the weapon. The governor of Väne cured Torbjörn Esgersson, apparently the son of Esger, took up his grandfather's weapon, the rear head, which he led in 1459 and later, as did his son Gudmund 
2 CONC Torbjörnsson, governor after the father 1486–1495, with whose daughter Forstena passed to the younger Forstena family. Whether there was a relationship between these and Sven Brynjulfsson, who carried the rear head, is unknown. Th
2 CONC e family has branched out into the gracious family Torstenson, no. 7. Another branch of the family has been introduced specifically with the name Ultfana.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Torbjörn Esgersson (gumsehuvud),''' born: 1420, Western Tunhem Älvsborg County.  Torbjörn married Ragnhild Svensdotter, daughter of Sven Johansson Jonsson Half Lilja and Ingeborg Toresdotter Byting. (Ragnhild Svensdotter died
2 CONC  in 1500 in Tunhem Älvsborg County. (P)
2 CONT
2 CONT =SDHK No: 19120=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters''' - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=+Esger+Torbj%C3%B6rnsson+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=+Esger+Torbj%C3%B6rnsson+&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_19120
2 CONC &tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating: 1418 July 11, of issue Forstena 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Content'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Esger Torbjörnsson gives his wife Ingrid Siggesdotter in the morning gift a farm in Faurås in Vinbergs sn and a farm in Okome, both in Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Post-medieval transcriptions:  Lars Sparre's copybook B 16 (J. 7), fol. 386v, ​​RA 0202
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter Text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thet scalom mannom witterlikt wara, which this breff see older hear, thet iak Äsger Thorbiörnson is confessed with thesso mino öpno brefue haffwa giffuit '''Ingridhe Siggadotter, my lovely wife,''' 2 farm in Hallande lying, one in
2 CONC  Fordese in Winberga sokn, to morning goofs, with fields and meadows, forests and all things in addition, vtan gardz and before, mooring and takno, with all the low lows and the grounds as wasgut law vtwijsa ok difference. ok if t
2 CONC hat happens, because we children together can catch, can honor the same morning when our children mothers ok ey fädherne; than can we so happen we children together get, then yoke the morning gaffes, which long leffwer. For more w
2 CONC isso here about bedi iak honest men's insignia hang for this letter with mino egno. Date Forsteno, anno Domini mcdxviii, feria secunda post octavas apostolorum Petri et Pauli,
2 CONT
2 CONT SEAL
2 CONT 2 pcs. avritade;
2 CONT
2 CONT N. 1. One heart (?) With circumference: s. Esger torbiornson; N. 2. Oxhufvud with circumference: p. Biorn .. orn. m. ds.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Forstenasläkten No. 2==
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble Forstenasläkten No. 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancient Frälsesläkt, introduced 1625. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The mödernet descended from the Abjörnsönernas (see the noble family of RAM AF Berga). Obtained at the introduction the name Forstenasläkten after its then main farm Forstena in Tunhems Parish, in Väne hundred Älvsborg County, whi
2 CONC ch, however, was only relatively late acquired. This farm was previously held by a law which in the gun initially brought a bagghuvud, which was later changed to a single-year-end. Of this older Forstena-Åro the following known. T
2 CONC he brothers Åke and Esger Torbjörn's sons perform during the years 1415 – 1435, the later married 1418 at Forstena with Ingrid, daughter of Gallowglass, the son of the Bagghuvud, who was named in the documents 1405 – 1417, and in 
2 CONC the weapon brought an in, and apparently owned Forstena (He was 1413 living in Väne hundred). Both of these brothers brought a oskaftated blade or heart into the weapon. Häradshövdingen in Väne County Torbjörn Esgersson, apparentl
2 CONC y the son of Esger, occupied the mother father's arms, Bagghuvudet, which he brought 1459 and later, as well as his son Gudmund Torbjörn's son, district Judge after the father in 1486 – 1495, with whose daughter Forstena transferr
2 CONC ed To the younger Forstena family. If any kinship existed between these and Sven Brynjulfsson, which brought Bagghuvudet, is not known. The family has branched out in the Grevliga dynasty, No. 7. Another branch of the dynasty has 
2 CONC been introduced specifically with the name Ultfana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source -'''''' Forstenasläkten nr 2'''''' -https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Forstenasl%C3%A4kten_nr_2 
