1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Torbjörn Esgersson Bjurum=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Profession: District Judge in Väne
2 CONT * Born: 1420 Forstena, Västra Tunhem, Västergötland, Sweden
2 CONT * Died: 1486 (66) Fjärås, Halland, Sweden
2 CONT * Son of Esger (Eskil) torbjörns son (s) and Ingrid daughter Bjurum husband to NN the father of • Gudmund torbjörns son Bjurum (Gudmund, born 1442 about Häradshöving in Väne County lived in Forstena in western Tunhem.)
2 CONT * Reer Torbjörn's son bjurum brother of Guttorm Esgersson (S-blade?) 
2 CONT * Owned 30 January 1459 Earth in Faruås Halland. Torbjörn Esgersson, son of Esger, occupied the mother father's weapon, Bagghuvudet, which he brought 1459 and later, as well as his son Gudmund Torbjörn's son, district Judge after 
2 CONC the Father 1486 – 1495.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Gudmund Torbjörnsson (gumsehuvud),''' Through Torsten Brunsson's marriage to Anna Gudmundsdotter, daughter of Gudmund Torbjörnsson (rear head of the older Forstenas family) and Ragnhild Svensdotter (half lily), Forstene trans
2 CONC itioned to the younger Forstenas family. Torsten Brunsson's sons: Göran Torstensson to Forstena and Nygård, horseman, the castle law at Gullberg Sealed the nobility's assurance of assurance and Gustav I's will Signed allegiance as
2 CONC surance to Erol XIV and his brother-in-law Peder Svenske in the Castle Act at Gullberg in 1573, joined at Dal Levde in 1590, when he signed the renewal of the estates by the inheritance association as well as the extension of the 
2 CONC succession to the women's line. Married after 1579 to his wife Elin Gudmundsdotter Children: Brown, Göran, Karin. Brun Göransson received King Sigismund's authority which appended to Dal. Married, had her daughter Anna. Göran Göra
2 CONC nsson. Married, daughter: Elin. Karin Göransdotter, married to Per Nilsson Kafl.
2 CONT *''' Reer Torbjörnsson (gumsehuvud),'''Född:	mellan 1450 och 1486 Västergötland, Sverige, Död:Bohuslän, Sverige, Son till Torbjörn Esgersson Gumsehuvud, Father of Torsten Reersson and brother of Gudmund Torbjörnsson Gumsehuvud
2 CONT
2 CONT =Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Directory of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/Sdhk_30992_30992.jpg#?c=&m=&s=&cv=&xywh=-972%2C-162%2C6310%2C3235 '''SDHK No: 30992''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1481 November 29, of issue, Geneved''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertil Petersson, Torbjörn Esgersson, Per Bonde and others . certifies that no one spoke on an empty "Glotzboder", which Jepp Krämare owned in "Geneveds" snow in Bjärke hd.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''  Original:  Or. Perg. RA 0101  pictures, Post-medieval regest / note:  Hellm. Misc. 65:24 (reg.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torbj%C3%B6rn+Esgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Torbj%C3%B6rn+Esgersson&AvanceradSok=True&page=2&postid=sdhk_44969&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab '''SDHK No: 44969''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1459 January 30, of issue Varberg Castle''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Torbjörn Esgersson in Forstena sells in open letter to the knight Åke Axelsson (Tott) in Hjuleberg 1 farm in Vinbergs parish and 1 farm in Okome in Lynga (Okome) parish. Furthermore ⅓, which was the inheritor's share of the father
2 CONC  and brother, in farms in Gisselstad in the Ljungby parish, Gödeby and the deserted Högryd with a mill in the Sibbarps parish, all in Faurås hearth, Kärragård in Spannarps parish in Himle hierad, a desert farm in Heberg in the yea
2 CONC r , Årstads hearth, 1 farm in Humlered in Kalvs parish, 1 farm in Tranebäck, 1 in Hjärtanäs (in the same parish), 1 in Ängasjö in (Ö.) Frölunda parish in Kinds hearth.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals together with Hans Vadde, mayor of Ny Varberg, Per Stud, mayor of Gamla Varberg, Nis Unge, Gottorm Gunnessen and Per Krok, mayors of Ny Varberg, as well as the mayor of Håkan Agessen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''' Original:  perg., Danish National Archives, Photocopy:  OAU, Uppsala; Sv. Diploma (digital image of OAU copy) Literature and commentary See SDHK no. 23183 (1439 12/4) where (probably the father) Esger Torbjörnsson se
2 CONC lls land to Åke Axelsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT For the sealants see A. Sandklef, Varberg's History (1963), pages 46 and 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://docplayer.se/24603233-Fran-sven-byrnjulfsson-och-elin-lindormsdotter-till-lennart-torstensson.html From Sven Byrnjulfsson and Elin Lindormsdotter to Lennart Torstensson]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3Forstena 1 Jönsson's death: then the children changed the legacy of their parents 3. Lindorm and Margita had the sons Jöns, Sixten and Bengt as well as the daughters Ingeborg, Elin and Kristina. Everyone used the lindorm seal ove
2 CONC r leaves. Jöns Lindormsson is believed to have died before February 1440, when a presumed son Lindorm Jönsson bought a farm 4. The farm Forstena in Väne hierad, which at the introduction of the knight's house in 1625 was given the
2 CONC  name of the family from Lindorm Jönsson's Sven Brynjulfsson family, lies between Hunneberg and the Göta River, along the road from Trollhättan to Vargön. At the beginning of the 14th century, Forstena was held by a family, which 
2 CONC carried in the arms an unshaft seabird, later replaced by a bag (gum) head. In this older Forstenas family were the years the brothers Åke and '''Esger Torgersson, of whom the latter in 1418 married Ingrid Siggesdotter. Torbjörn E
2 CONC sgersson was county governor in Väne here. When his granddaughter Anna Gudmundsdotter married Torsten Brunsson (see below),'''  Forstena moved on to the later nobility and in 1625 introduced the younger Forstenas family. Lindorm J
2 CONC önsson This younger Forstenas family originated from Jöns Abjörnsson's fourth son, the gunman Lindorm Jönsson (spar over leaves), born at the latest in 1365 and before 1400 married to Margita (Margareta) Sixtensdotter, daughter of
2 CONC  the district governor in Vartofta, inherited Sixten Martinsson. Margita died on December 23, 1407, when Lindorm chose a camp town for her and herself in Vadstena Monastery 2. On March 26, 1418, Lindorm Sixten Lindormsson was also
2 CONC  the leader among the brothers. He was church pastor in Tingvalla (where Karlstad was founded) and in 1436 was also called prost in all of Värmland. After Lindorm's death, Sixten appears to be the head of the family. There is no i
2 CONC ndication of marriage, so Helge and Tyrgil's Sons of Sons, mentioned in a letter 1440, may have been the sons of another Sixten. In March 1344, Sixten and his cousins ​​confirmed his deceased uncle Magnus's gifts to Vadstena Monas
2 CONC tery 5. After that, Sixten is no longer mentioned. Bengt Lindormsson. If he is only known that he participated in the succession after the parents Ingeborg Lindormsdotter mortgaged a farm 6 in Vallerstad, Kärda sn, Östbo hereafter
2 CONC , apparently widow after his end knew husband Olof Kärling, possibly belonging to the family of Sigge Djäkns brother Nils ( 64: 3). Kristina Lindormsdotter was inaugurated on January 13, 1415 to the nun in Vadstena, where the fath
2 CONC er donated, among other things. Torbjörnatorp in Vartofta herad. Kristina passed away on March 9 Elin Lindormsdotter married (after 1418 (but before 1440) with Sven Bryn- 3 SDHK Skara 4 SDHK Vadstena 1 SAÄ II:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' From Sven Byrnjulfsson and Elin Lindormsdotter to Lennart Torstensson 
