1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingeborg Pedersdotter (Sparre)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Peder (Bonde) Larsson (Sparre af Rossvik) and Ingegerd Toresdotter Byting, Till Stola
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_af_Rossvik_nr_7 Noble family Sparre af Rossvik no. 7, by Adelsvapen Geneologies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 3'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peder Larsson , (son of Lars Siggesson''', Tab. 2), to Stola in Strö parish Skaraborg county, which he obtained with his 1st wife. Called Peder Bonde 4 , gunsmith. Lived in 1481, but was dead in 1490 7 . '''Married 1st to Ingeg
2 CONC erd Tordsdotter , died before 1485, daughter of Tord Pyting to Stola and Holmfrid Johansdotter Broka Married 2nd 7 to Ragnhild Turesdotter , who lived as a widow in 1493, daughter of the knight and lawman in Västergötland Ture Jön
2 CONC sson ( Black Skåning ) and Birgitta Henrik's daughter Snakenborg.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Ingeborg Pedersdotter ,''' died before 1503. Married before 1485 to the squire and district chief Peder Bengtsson Gylta , to Påtorp, in his 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1503 to Christina Torstensdotter) 7 , died 1527.
2 CONT * 1. '''Nils Pedersson .''' Armsman 1485–1493. Unmarried beaten in Uppsala. 7
2 CONT * 1. '''Ingegerd Pedersdotter .''' Nun 5 (probably in Gudhem's monastery).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gylta&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=19&postid=sdhk_31598&tab=post SDHK no: 31598]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1485 June 7, Place of issue: Croft'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Armsman Peder Bengtsson (Gylta) , in the presence of Abraham Kristiernsson and Lindorm Mattsson, gives Sigge Larsson in Skofteby a receipt for his wife's inheritance, which he had in his care as guardian.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals together with (Abraham Kristiernsson and Lindorm Mattsson).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Source:''' Post-medieval copies:  Lars Eriksson Sparre's copy book, hs B 16, fol. 220r, National Archives (SE/RA/0202) image ; prints of B 16 texts, Swedish Diplomatarium
2 CONT Literature and commentary
2 CONT
2 CONT About Peder Bengtsson Gylta and his wife Ingeborg Pedersdotter see ÄSF II, p. 36, as well as Elgenstierna, Sparre af Rossvik, p. 401 (tab. 3); about Sigge Larsson see Elgenstierna, a.st., (tab. 4). Cf. SDHK no. 32543 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gylta&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=19&postid=sdhk_32543&tab=post#tab SDHK no: 32543]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1491 January 10, Place of issue: Skofteby'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Armsman Nils Petersson issues a letter of receipt to his uncle Sigge Larsson, who after the death of the issuer's father Peter Bonde had his inheritance in custody. Nils Petersson declares a letter (1485 7/6, SDHK no. 31598 ) as d
2 CONC ead, which letter his brother-in-law Peter Bengtsson (Gylta) held; in addition, Nils confirms his paper letter (1490 26/1, SDHK no. 32375 ), which he gave to his uncle during the time he served Mr. Hans Åkesson, who sealed said pa
2 CONC per letter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer asks Bishop Brynolf in Skara, the dean master Olof, master Håkan Mörk, penitentiary in Skara, and the well-to-do man Jöns Knutsson to seal together with himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Post-medieval copies:  Lars Eriksson Sparre's copy book, hs B 16, fol. 94v-95r, no. 148, Riksarkivet (SE/RA/0202) picture ; prints of B 16 texts, Sv. Dipl. Literature and commentary, An odat. receipt for chattels 
2 CONC and letters has been attached to this letter, see SDHK no. 32544
