1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Björn Pedersson (Bååt)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Peder Erlandsson (Bååt) and Märta Björnsdotter (pukehorn) af Ulfsunda 
2 CONT
2 CONT Björn Pedersson (son of Peder Erlandsson, the elder), to Fållnäs. National Council of 1547-1560. Death 1570-06-01. Married 1: o 1528 with Brita Nilsdotter, daughter of the Knight, Riksrådet and Östgötalagmannen Nils Bosson (Grip) 
2 CONC and Anna Trolle nr 36. Married 2: o with Christina Krumme, daughter of the knight, the council and the statue holder at Stockholm Castle Nils Nilsson Krumme, to Örboholm and Gesterby, and Margareta Siggesdotter (Sparre).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouses==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (1). Brita Nilsdotter  (yngre Grip), daughter of the Knight, Riksrådet and Östgötalagmannen Nils Bosson (Grip) and Anna Trolle nr 36
2 CONT * Married (2). Christina Krumme, daughter of the knight, the council and the statue holder at Stockholm Castle Nils Nilsson Krumme, to Örboholm and Gesterby, and Margareta Siggesdotter (Sparre).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children with Brita Nilsdotter  (yngre Grip)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marta Björnsdotter, died young
2 CONT * Nils Björnsson, died young
2 CONT * Lars Björnsson, died young
2 CONT * Nis Björnsson, died young
2 CONT * Marta Björnsdotter, died young
2 CONT * Brita Björnsdotter, died in 1592 according to the tombstone of Almunge church, Stockholm County, where she and her 2nd husband are buried. Married 1: o with Johan Mattsson (archbold), to Harön in Bro socken, Stockholm County, by
2 CONC  a 1581-06-11 adlad, but not introd. Att. Married 2: o with Christer Carlsson Månesköld.
2 CONT * Jakob Björnsson. Ståthållare. 
2 CONT * Erland Björnsson, to Skattmansö in Vittinge parish and Aspenäs in Östervåla parish both in Västmanland county. Signed 1582 years of parliamentary decision and legacy association 1590-03-07. Stand Holder Over Salberget 1607-12-08
2 CONC . Riksråd 1609. Again stand-stand over Salberg County (Ash.) 1613-06-20. Court of Appeals in Svea Court of Appeal Married 1: o with her mother's cousin Beata Trolle, daughter of the council Ture Arvidsson Trolle, to Eknaholm and B
2 CONC ergkvara, etc., and Magdalena Eriksdotter (Gyllenstierna). Married 2: o 1603-01-09 with Margareta Lagesdotter Posse. Probably they had double weddings with her sister Märta Lagesdotter Posse. Daughter of the chief executive Make A
2 CONC xelsson Posse and his 2nd wife Anna Trolle.
2 CONT * Gustaf Björnsson. Riksråd. Death 1594. 
2 CONT * Anna Björnsdotter. Married to fence Arent Joensson (Gyllenhorn).
2 CONT * Peter Björnsson
2 CONT * Margaretha Björnsdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children with Christina Krumme:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Magdalena Björnsdotter. Married 1: o 1577 with chambermaid Erik Andersson (Ekeblad). Married 2: o with Torstsen Christoffersson (Forstenasläkten).
2 CONT * Boo Björnsson, died young
2 CONT * Jons Björnsson, died young
2 CONT * Marta Björnsdotter, died Young
2 CONT
2 CONT ==History of the  (Bååt) Families ==
2 CONT
2 CONT The boat is an old Swedish salvation law derived from Småland. The shield, a boat, gave rise to the ethnic name, but only in the early 1600s, a couple of men-ages before the expulsion of the eternal people were taken up by the mem
2 CONC bers. The pedigree can not be fully assured anymore than to Jon Petersson, a resident of Flöxhult, as mentioned in the documents from 1390-1418. Since her mother, Kristina Hemmingsdotter, had been married to a knight before her la
2 CONC st marriage with Jens Brudsson (Lions face), last 1351, and her newly-born son was born in this earlier marriage, it is very close to suppose that her first husband and Jon Petersson's father was identical to that of King Magnus E
2 CONC riksson's known knight Peter Jonsson, who also carried the boat and was a resident of Småland. The latter would therefore be considered as the ancestor's ancestor. Obviously, close to the Farmers 'Nest (compare the article Bonde, 
2 CONC Family Overview) - he himself sometimes called Peter Bonde (and Peter Haak) - this Mr. Peter Jonsson is referred to as the National Council of 1322 and won by King Magnus' Reward 1336 rider battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bååt nr 3 Geneology - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bååt_nr_3, Helt andra uppgifter finns kring barn. Min Ana finns med, men med olika uppgifter kring modern/ 
2 CONT
