0 @N6000000002187592846@ NOTE Adela Capet
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Adela of Flanders (1009-June 5, 1063) was the Countess of Contenance, later the Countess of Flanders, and second daughter of Robert II of France (Robert le Pieux) and Constance of Arles. Her first husband, Richard III of Normandy 
1 CONC (997 - 1027), had a short and inconsequential reign over the Duchy of Normandy before dying under mysterious circumstances in 1027. They did not have any children together, though Richard had two illegitimate children by unknown m
1 CONC istresses.
1 CONT
1 CONT Adela married Baldwin V of Flanders (d.September 1, 1067) in 1028 and encouraged her husband to rebel against his father, Baldwin IV of Flanders. Her efforts failed, and Baldwin V did not become Count of Flanders until his father'
1 CONC s death in 1035. Baldwin and Adela had four children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Baldwin VI, 1030-1070
1 CONT     * Matilda of Flanders, c.1031-1083 who married William the Conqueror
1 CONT     * Robert I of Flanders, c.1033–1093
1 CONT     * Henry of Flanders c.1035
