1 CONT Adèle’s influence lay mainly in her family connections. On the death of her brother, Henry I of France, the guardianship of his seven-year-old son Philip I fell jointly the boy's mother and to Adèle’s husband so that from 1060 to 
1 CONC 1067, they were Regents of France.
