0 @N6000000001353866787@ NOTE AKA Baldwin I, Count of Hainault
0 @N6000000001540958519@ NOTE Baldwin VI, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Baldwin VI of Flanders (c. 1030 ? July 17, 1070) was briefly Count ofFlanders, from 1067 to 1070. He was also (as Baldwin I) count of Hainaut from 1051 to 1070.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the eldest son of Baldwin V of Flanders and Adele Capet, a daughter of king Robert II of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History and Family
1 CONT In 1051 he married Richilde, Countess of Mons and Hainaut, widow of count Herman of Mons. By this marriage Flanders took control of Hainaut(at that moment still a conglomerate of the county of Mons, the margraviate of Valenciennes
1 CONC  and the southern part of the landgraviate of Brabant).
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin's early death left Flanders and Hainaut in the hands of his young son Arnulf III, with Richilde as regent. The countship was soon usurped by Baldwin's brother Robert the Frisian, who became count Robert I of Flanders. The 
1 CONC young Arnulf III was killed the next year at theBattle of Cassel and Baldwin's younger son eventually became Baldwin II of Hainaut.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT Counts of Flanders family tree
1 CONT Counts of Hainaut family tree
1 CONT Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Line 163-23
