0 @N6000000002187746698@ NOTE Floris I, Count of Holland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Floris I of Holland (1017 in Vlaardingen, Zuid Holland, Netherlands - June 28, 1061 in Gelderland, Netherlands) was Count of Holland from 1049 to 1061. He was a son of Dirk III and Othelindis of Nordmark.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was murdered.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married ca. 1050 Princess Gertrude of Saxony, daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt, and had seven children by her:
1 CONT
1 CONT Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liége. 
1 CONT Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17 June 1091). 
1 CONT Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége. 
1 CONT Bertha (*ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072. 
1 CONT Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége. 
1 CONT Machteld (b. ca. 1057) 
1 CONT Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guines. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Dirk IV Count of Holland
1 CONT 1049 - 1061 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Dirk V 
0 @N6000000003051219809@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Floris I, Count of Holland", retrieved 13 Oct 07]
1 CONT Floris I of Holland (also called Florent I) born (1017 in Vlaardingen, Zuid Holland, Netherlands - June 28, 1061 in Gelderland, Netherlands) was Count of Holland (which was called Frisia at that time) from 1049 to 1061. He was a s
1 CONC on of Dirk III and Othelindis of Nordmark.
1 CONT
1 CONT He succeeded his brother Dirk IV who was murdered in 1049. He was involved in a war of a few Lotharingian vassals against the imperial authority.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was murdered.
1 CONT
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married ca. 1050 Princess Gertrude of Saxony, daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt, and had seven children by her:
1 CONT
1 CONT - Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liege.
1 CONT - Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen?17 June 1091).
1 CONT - Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége.
1 CONT - Bertha (ca. 1055?1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072.
1 CONT - Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége.
1 CONT - Machteld (b. ca. 1057)
1 CONT - Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guînes.
0 @N6000000003949776950@ NOTE Count Floris I, who succeeded Dirk IV in 1049, continued Holland's expansion southwards. In 1061 he was victorious in a battle against Ecbert I of Friesland near Nederhemert, but afterwards Count Floris was killed there while rest
1 CONC ing under a tree, probably on orders from Emperor Heinrich IV of Germany. (According to one of my sources, Floris' physical remains show that he was a giant of over 2 meters tall.)
