0 @N6000000002187746679@ NOTE Dirk V, Count of Holland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk V (1052 – June 17, 1091), was Count of Holland from 1061 to 1091.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk V succeeded Floris I, under the guardianship of his mother, Gertrude of Saxony. William, Bishop of Utrecht, took advantage of the young ruler, occupying territory that he had claimed in Holland. William's claim was confirmed 
1 CONC by two charters of the emperor Henry IV. (April 30, 1064 and May 2, 1064). Dirk only retained possession of lands west of the Vlie and around the mouths of the Rhine.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gertrude and her son withdrew to the islands of Frisia (Zeeland), leaving William to occupy the disputed lands. In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian), the second son of Baldwin V of Flanders. Robert gave
1 CONC  Dirk the Imperial Flanders as an appanage - including the islands of Frisia west of the Frisian Scheldt. He then became his stepson's guardian, gaining control of the islands east of the Scheldt.
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert therefore, in both his own right and that of Dirk, was now the ruler of all Frisia. The death of his brother Baldwin VI in 1070 led to civil war in Flanders. The claim of Robert to the guardianship of his nephew Arnulf III 
1 CONC was disputed by Richilda, the widow of Baldwin VI. The issue was decided by Robert's victory at Cassel (February 1071), where Arnulf was killed and Richilda taken prisoner.
1 CONT
1 CONT While Robert was thus engaged in Flanders, an effort was made to recover the County of Holland and other lands now held by William of Utrecht. The people rose in revolt, but were brought back under Episcopal rule by an army under 
1 CONC the command of Godfrey IV (the Hunchback), duke of Lower Lorraine, by order of the emperor (Henry IV). In 1076, at the request of William, Duke Godfrey visited his domains in the Frisian borderland. At Delft, the duke was murdered
1 CONC  by revolutionaries (February 26, 1076). William of Utrecht died on April 17, 1076.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk V, now managing his own estate, was quick to take advantage of this favorable juncture. With the help of Robert (his stepfather) he raised an army and besieged Conrad of Utrecht, the successor of William, in the castle of Yss
1 CONC elmonde, taking him prisoner. The bishop purchased his liberty by surrendering all claim to the disputed lands.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk V was succeeded by Floris II upon his death in 1091.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Floris I Count of Holland
1 CONT 1061–1091 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Floris II 
0 @N6000000004664142272@ NOTE
1 CONT HM George I's 16-Great Grandfather.       Lady Diana's 25-Great Grandfather.       PM Churchill's 24-Great Grandfather.       Geo Washington's 21-Great Grandfather.
