1 CONC dered by revolutionaries (February 26, 1076). William of Utrecht died on April 17, 1076.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dirk V, now managing his own estate, was quick to take advantage of th is favorable juncture. With the help of Robert (his stepfather) he rai sed an army and besieged Conrad of Utrecht, the successor of William,i n the castle of Y
1 CONC sselmonde, taking him prisoner. The bishop purchased his liberty by surrendering all claim to the disputed lands.  DirkV wa s succeeded by Floris II upon his death in 1091.
